hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4801","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, saying: I asked Aishah: Who was dearest to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: Abu Bakr, then Umar, then Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."
"4802","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Jabir ibn al-Subh who said: Umaynah and Zaynab, his aunts, narrated to me that they met Aishah among women, and a woman asked her about drinks. She said: I do not permit nabidh of hantam, nor naqir, nor muzaffat, and I forbid only what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade."
"4803","Musa narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Jabir ibn al-Subh who said: I heard Khilas al-Hajari saying: I heard Aishah say: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would spend the night in one blanket while I was menstruating; if anything got on him he washed that spot, no more, then prayed in it."
"4804","Musa narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrating from Dhakwan Abu Amr, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Consult women about their private parts, for the virgin is shy and stays silent, and that is her permission."
"4805","Musa narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Abu Hazrah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: We were with Aishah when food was brought, and al-Qasim stood to pray. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None prays with food present, nor while holding back the two filths."
"4806","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, Qays narrated to us, from Abu Sahlah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Call one of my companions for me. I said: Abu Bakr? He said: No. I said: Umar? He said: No. I said: Your cousin Ali? He said: No. I said: Whom? He said: Uthman. When he came he said: Step aside, and he spoke to him privately while Uthman's color changed. When the day of the house came and he was besieged, we said: O Commander of the Believers, will you not fight? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me a pledge, and I am holding myself to it."
"4807","Musa ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Aishah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No Muslim dies and a community of Muslims prays over him reaching a hundred, interceding for him, except they are granted intercession for him."
"4808","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the people during his illness sitting, so they stood, and he gestured to them, and they sat. Then he said: The imam is only followed; when he bows, bow, when he prostrates, prostrate, and when he prays sitting, pray sitting."
"4809","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah who said: Sawdah was a large, slow woman, so she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for permission to pour forth from Muzdalifah at night, and he permitted her. Aishah said: I wish I had asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Sawdah asked him. Ayyub said: Aishah would only pour forth with the imam."
"4810","Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab said: I heard Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim reported to me, that Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr reported to him, that Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him that he heard Aishah saying: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am burnt. He asked him what was wrong. He said: I broke fast in Ramadan. Then he sat, and there was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a large basket called al-araq containing dates. He said: Where is the burnt one? He stood, and he said: Give it in charity."
"4811","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to order one of us when menstruating to wrap herself, then he would touch her."
"4812","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Aishah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a sick person or a sick person was brought to him, he said: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, You are the Healer, a healing that leaves no illness."
"4813","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling nor two do not make unlawful."
"4814","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Malik al-Makki, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only meant by al-usaylah: intercourse."
"4815","And with it he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling nor two do not make unlawful."
"4816","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Harmalah reported to me, from Ata and Sulayman sons of Yasar, and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was lying in his house with his thighs - or shins - uncovered. Abu Bakr asked permission and he permitted him in that state, and he spoke. Then Umar asked permission and he permitted him likewise, and he spoke. Then Uthman asked permission, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and straightened his clothes - Muhammad said: I do not say that in one day - and he entered and spoke. When he left, Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr entered and you did not sit nor care, then Umar entered and you showed no joy nor care. Then Uthman entered and you sat and straightened your clothes. He said: Should I not be shy of a man the angels are shy of?"
"4817","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, Muhammad reported to me, Abu Salamah reported to me, that he asked Aishah about the two prostrations the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray after Asr. She said: He used to pray them, then he was distracted from them or forgot them, so he prayed them after Asr, then kept them, and when he prayed a prayer he kept it. Abu Zakariya said: Ismail said: Meaning: he persisted in it."
"4818","Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Saad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah who said: When I parted the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I split his parting from his crown, letting his forelock fall between his eyes. Allah knows whether that was because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We do not hold back hair nor garment? Or was it a mark he marked himself with? Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr - a learned Muslim - told me: It is but a mark of the marks of the prophets, which the Christians alone among people held to."
"4819","Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Saad narrated to us, from his father, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, Yahya ibn Said ibn al-As reported to me, that Said ibn al-As reported to him: That Uthman and Aishah narrated to him, that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq asked permission of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was lying on his bed wearing Aishah's cloak. He permitted Abu Bakr in that state. He said: He fulfilled his need to him, then left. Uthman said: Then Umar asked permission, and he permitted him in that state, and he fulfilled his need to him, then left. He said: Aishah said: I did not see you rush for Abu Bakr and Umar as you rushed for Uthman? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Uthman is a shy man; I feared if I permitted him in that state he would not fully state his need."
"4820","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed while she lay across to his right and left."
"4821","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while she lay across in front of him."
"4822","Hudbah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution, then kiss, then pray, without renewing ablution."
"4823","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Saad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father who said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not marry me until Gabriel came to him with my image and said: This is your wife. He married me while I was a girl wearing hawf, and when he married me Allah cast modesty upon me."
"4824","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us, from Ibn Harmalah, from Abdullah ibn Niyar, from Urwah, from Aishah, that a man asked permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard his voice he said: What an evil man, what an evil son of the tribe. When he entered, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cheerful to him. When he left, Aishah spoke to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you said: What an evil man, what an evil son of the tribe, then when he entered you were cheerful to him? He said: O Aishah, among the worst people are those feared for their foulness."
"4825","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Zaidah, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never raised his head to the sky except he said: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your obedience."
"4826","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Ibn Zurarah to be cauterized."
"4827","Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to give people their stations."
"4828","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Hasan ibn Muhammad who said: Aishah said: A piece of gazelle was given to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram, and he returned it and did not eat it."
"4829","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three Sahuli garments, a grave niche was made for him, and bricks were set over him upright."
"4830","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith reported to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) screening me with his garment while I looked at the Abyssinians playing, I being a girl. So estimate the young ignorant girl of recent age. She said: It was a feast day; the Sudanese played with shields and spears. Either I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or he said: Do you wish to watch? I said: Yes. So he set me behind him, my cheek on his cheek, saying: Go on, sons of Arfidah, until when I tired he said: Enough? I said: Yes. He said: Then go."
"4831","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to me, Bakr ibn Mudar reported to me, from Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, similar. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Enough? I said: Do not hurry, O Messenger of Allah. She said: I had no love of looking at them, but I wanted women to know his standing and my place with him."
"4832","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, and Sharik reported to me, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Aishah, that she said: Whenever it was her night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out at the end of the night to al-Baqi and say: Peace be upon you, abode of believing people; what you were promised has come to you, deferred till tomorrow, and we, if Allah wills, shall join you; O Allah, forgive the people of Baqi al-Farqad."
"4833","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Abdullah ibn Niyar, from Urwah, from Aishah, that a man asked permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Who is this? They said: So-and-so. He said: What an evil man and evil son of the tribe - or as he said - admit him. When he entered he was cheerful to him. Aishah said: You said: What an evil man and evil son of the tribe, then you were cheerful to him? He said: O Aishah, the worst people before Allah on the Day of Resurrection are those people leave fearing their evil."
"4834","Zakariya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah who said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at his ihram, and saw the perfume in his parting after three days while he was in ihram."
"4835","Zakariya narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not perform ablution after bathing."
"4836","Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Saad narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never found me at dawn except sleeping."
"4837","Zakariya narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amrah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The thief's hand is cut for a quarter dinar and up."
"4838","Kamil ibn Talhah narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Jafar ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman married without her guardian's permission, her marriage is void; if he consummated with her, she gets her dowry for what he took of her private part, and if they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"4839","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said narrated to us, Uqayl and Yunus narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of my nation takes a debt then strives to repay it, then dies before repaying it, I am his guardian."
"4840","Harun narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr reported to me, that Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to him, that Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to him, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man recited this verse: Whoever does evil is recompensed for it. He said: Are we recompensed for all we did? We are ruined then. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Yes, the believer is recompensed for it in this world, in his affliction in his body, in what harms him."
"4841","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Musab ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Face the qiblah closely."
"4842","Kamil narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he stood with the people in the mosque, and they lined behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood long in the day until men fell from heat, until I saw men splashing water on their faces, then he bowed like his standing, until I saw men falling too, then he raised his head, then prostrated, then stood shorter than his first standing, then bowed shorter than his first bowing, then raised his head, then prostrated, then stood again shorter than that, then bowed, then raised his head, then prostrated."
"4843","Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Nuaym al-Hadrami, from Muslim ibn Mikhraq who said: I said to Aishah, Mother of the Believers: Some people, one of them reads the Quran twice or thrice in a night. She said: Those read but did not really read; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand the whole night reciting al-Baqarah, Al Imran, and al-Nisa, not passing a verse of glad tidings except he supplicated."
"4844","Kamil narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died of pleurisy."
"4845","Kamil narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid prayer when the sun rises until it is high, saying: It rises with the horn of Satan, and forbid prayer when it nears setting until it sets."
"4846","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Ibn Shaqiq, and he is Abdullah, who said: I asked Aisha about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: He used to pray four before Zuhr, then go out and pray Zuhr, then return and pray two rakahs, then go out for Maghrib, then return and pray two rakahs, then go out for Isha, then return and pray two rakahs."
"4847","Saeed ibn Yahya ibn Saeed al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Zakariya narrated to us, from Hurayth, from Amir, from Masruq, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes bathe from janaba, then come to me and I would embrace him to me, and I would warm him, and I had not bathed after him."
"4848","Saeed ibn Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Saeed, from Mujahid, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in his house like one of you in his house; he would stitch his garment and work as one of you works."
"4849","Saeed ibn Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: This is what we read to Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha who said: (He frowned and turned away) was revealed concerning Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man. He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and kept saying: O Messenger of Allah, guide me, while with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were some of the chiefs of the polytheists, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept turning away from him and turning to the others, saying: Do you see any harm in what I say? And they would say: No. So concerning this was revealed: (He frowned and turned away)."
"4850","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, the brother of Hajjaj, narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Zurara, from Saad ibn Hisham, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The two rakahs before Fajr are better than the world and what is in it."
"4851","Abu Saeed al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abu Yaqub al-Tawam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Mulayka narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated, then Umar followed him with a small vessel of water, and he said: What is this, O Umar? He said: Water for you to perform ablution with, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have not been commanded to perform ablution every time I urinate, and if I did so it would become a sunna."
"4852","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha narrated to us, from his father, from Masruq, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) indeed used to love beginning with the right in his purification when he purified himself, and in his combing when he combed, and in putting on his shoes when he put them on."
"4853","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Saeed, from Abu Mashar, from al-Nakhai, from al-Aswad, from Aisha who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send the sacrificial animals and twist their garlands, then he would not avoid what the one in ihram avoids."
"4854","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amra, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) garlanded his sacrificial animal and marked it, and sent it with Abu Bakr, then he did not give up anything that Allah had made lawful until the sacrificial animal was slaughtered."
"4855","Abu Musa narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Saeed, from Abu Mashar, from al-Nakhai, from al-Aswad, from Aisha who said: I used to rub it off the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); if you see it, wash it, and if not, sprinkle it."
"4856","Abu Musa narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Saeed, from Abu Mashar, from al-Nakhai, from al-Aswad, from Aisha who said: When he wanted to bathe from janaba, he would begin with his hands and wash them, then wash his private areas and pour water over them, and when he had cleaned, he would rub them against a wall, then proceed to ablution, then pour water over his head."
"4857","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabia, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sleepless one night, then said: Would that a righteous man from my companions would come and guard me tonight. She said: Then we heard the sound of weapons, and he said: Who is this? He said: I am Saad ibn Abi Waqqas; I have come to guard you. She said: Then he slept until I heard his snoring."
"4858","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ghaniya narrated to us, from his father, from al-Shaybani, from Jumay ibn Umayr who said: I entered with my mother upon Aisha, and she asked her about Ali, and she said: I have not seen a man more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than him, nor a woman more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than his wife."
"4859","Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Safiya bint Shayba, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe with about a sa of water and perform ablution with about a mudd."
"4860","Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Muadha al-Adawiya, from Aisha that she said: Tell your husbands to wash away from themselves the trace of stool and urine, for I am shy to command them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do so."
"4861","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Labid, he heard Abu Salama saying: I came to Aisha and said: O mother, inform me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: His night prayer in Ramadan and otherwise was thirteen rakahs, including the two rakahs of Fajr. I said: Inform me about his fasting. She said: He would fast until we would say: He has fasted, and he would break fast until we would say: He has broken fast, and I never saw him fast in any month more than his fasting in Shaban; he would fast all of Shaban; he would fast Shaban except a little."
"4862","Abu al-Fadl said: And I heard Sufyan saying: She, meaning Aisha, said: I would have fasting due from Ramadan, and I would not make it up until Shaban, all of it out of reluctance to fast apart from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as Sufyan explained it."
"4863","Hudba narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadala narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Saad ibn Hisham ibn Amir who said: I was a man who followed rulers, so my father seized me and confined me - Mubarak said: and I do not know but that he said: and shackled me - and said to me: By Allah, you shall not go out until you memorize the Book of Allah by heart. So I memorized the Book of Allah by heart, and Allah benefited me by it, and the world left me, and I came to dislike marrying and engaging in worldly activity. So I entered upon Aisha and said: Saad ibn Hisham ibn Amir. She said: May Allah have mercy on Amir; he was struck as a martyr on the day of Uhud. He said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, I want to devote myself to worship without marriage, so I have come to ask you about that. She said: O Hisham, do not remain celibate, for Allah said: (You have in the Messenger of Allah a good example), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married and children were born to him. He said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, tell me about the character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: O my son, do you not read the Quran? Allah said: (And you are upon a great character); the character of Muhammad was the Quran. He said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, tell me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: O my son, who can bear the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, he would pray two rakahs, then sleep a short sleep, then rise and pray two rakahs, and two, and two, and two, and two, and one rakah - or she said: he would pray two and two and two and two and one rakah - a prayer after Isha of nine rakahs, and eleven; then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grew bulky and his flesh increased, he prayed two and two and one, and prayed two while sitting."
"4864","Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me that Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to him, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad who narrated to him, that Aisha narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."
"4865","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, from Haritha ibn Muhammad, from Amra, from Aisha who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand for ablution, he would tilt the vessel and mention the name of Allah, then complete the ablution."
"4866","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Sadaqa ibn Saeed, from Jumay ibn Umayr, that his mother and his maternal aunt entered upon Aisha and said: O Mother of the Believers, what would one of you do when she menstruated? She said: She would tie a waist-wrapper over herself, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would embrace her belly and what is above that. They said: How does he bathe? She said: He pours water over his hands, then cleans himself, then strikes the ground with his hand, then pours water over his head three times. She said: As for us, we pour five times because of the braids. They said: Inform us about Ali. She said: What do you ask about a man whose hand was placed in such a place from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so his soul flowed out into his hand, and he wiped his face with it? And they differed about his burial, so he said: The most beloved spot to Allah is the place where His prophet died. They said: Then why did you go out against him? She said: A matter decreed; I would wish to ransom it with all that is on earth."
"4867","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Umm Dharra, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I and the guardian of the orphan will be in Paradise like these two - and he joined the index and middle fingers - and the one who strives for the orphan, the widow, and the poor is like the striving warrior in the path of Allah, and like the fasting one standing in prayer who does not tire."
"4868","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make some of your prayers in your houses."
"4869","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim who said: Aisha passed by a water belonging to Banu Amir called al-Hawab, and the dogs barked at her, so she said: What is this? They said: A water belonging to Banu Amir. She said: Turn me back, turn me back; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: What about one of you when the dogs of al-Hawab bark at her?"
"4870","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Saman, from Saeed ibn Abi Saeed al-Maqburi, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Aisha who said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who steps with his sandals in filth. He said: The dust is purification for them."
"4871","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Umara ibn Abi Hafsa narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Aisha who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about Ibn Judan. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What was he? She said: I said: He used to slaughter fat camels, honor the neighbor, host the guest, speak truthfully, fulfill covenants, uphold kinship, free the captive, feed food, and render trusts. He said: Did he ever say even one day: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the Fire of Hell? She said: No, and he did not know what Hell was. He said: Then no."
"4872","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Bistam ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah Yazid ibn Humayd, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, that Aisha came one day from the graveyard, so I said to her: Where have you come from, O Mother of the Believers? She said: From the grave of my brother Abd al-Rahman. I said to her: O Mother of the Believers, did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid visiting graves? She said: Yes, he had forbidden visiting them, and he had forbidden sacrificial meat to be eaten beyond three days, then he commanded eating it, and he had forbidden drinking nabidh from jars."
"4873","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Aban ibn Sama narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Aisha who said: I and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe from a single vessel, he beginning before me."
"4874","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Layth ibn Saad, from Muawiya ibn Salih, from Yahya ibn Saeed, from Amra who said: It was said to Aisha: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do in his house? She said: He was a human being among human beings; he would delouse his garment, milk his sheep, and serve himself."
"4875","Abu Talib Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to me, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No Muslim dies and a community of Muslims reaching a hundred pray over him and intercede for him, except they are granted intercession for him."
"4876","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Thawab, a man of Yamama, narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Fadi narrated to me, from his father, from Sayf ibn Abdullah al-Himyari who said: I entered with some men with me upon Aisha, and we asked her about a man touching his private part. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I do not care whether I touched it or my nose."
"4877","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, that she was asked: What did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do in his house? She said: He would stitch his garment, repair his sandal, and do what men do in their houses."
"4878","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, that she was asked about the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He would pray sitting; when he wanted to bow, he would stand and recite thirty verses or forty verses, then bow and prostrate."
"4879","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, and Muawiya ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu Hamza narrated to me, from Aisha, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sleeping before Isha, nor engaging in idle talk after it; either remembering, so he gains, or sleeping, so he is safe."
"4880","Muawiya said: And Abu Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to me, from Aisha, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Night conversation is for three: for a bridegroom, or a traveler, or one keeping night vigil."
"4881","Al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulayka who said: It reached Aisha about a woman wearing sandals, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the mannishness of women."
"4882","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiya narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Malik al-Makki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Mulayka narrated to us, from Aisha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-usayla is intercourse."
"4883","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was bewitched until it seemed to him that he had done something though he had not done it, until one day, while he was with me, he supplicated to Allah and supplicated, then said: Did you know, O Aisha, that Allah has given me a ruling concerning what I sought His ruling about? I said: What is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Two angels came to me; one sat at my head and the other at my feet. Then one of them said to his companion: What ails the man? He said: Bewitched. He said: Who bewitched him? He said: Labid ibn al-Asam, the Jew from Banu Zurayq. He said: In what? He said: In a comb and combings. He said: Where is it? He said: In the well of Dhi Arwan. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went with some of his companions to the well, looked at it and its palms, then returned to Aisha and said: By Allah, its water is as if infused with henna, and its palms as if the heads of devils. I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you take it out? He said: No; as for me, Allah has cured me and healed me, and I feared to stir up evil for people from it, so he ordered that it be buried."
"4884","Al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Fudayl Abu Muadh narrated to us, from Abu Hariz, from al-Shabi, from Aisha, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to marry a woman from his wives, he would say: So-and-so son of so-and-so proposes to so-and-so daughter of so-and-so."
"4885","Abdullah ibn Muti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Awwam, from one who narrated to him, from Aisha who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) founded the mosque of Medina, he brought a stone and placed it, and Abu Bakr brought a stone and placed it, and Umar brought a stone and placed it, and Uthman brought a stone and placed it. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about that, and he said: This is the order of the caliphate after me."
"4886","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Urwa, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite while sitting; when he wanted to bow, he would stand for about as long as a person recites forty verses."
"4887","Mujahid narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik narrated to us, from Umar ibn Suwayd ibn Ghaylan al-Thaqafi, from Aisha bint Talha, from Aisha, Mother of the Believers, who said: We used to go out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having perfumed ourselves with saffron and wars, and we had entered ihram; then we would sweat and it would flow over our faces, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would see it and not reproach us for it."
"4888","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, al-Jurayri Abu Masud narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq who said: I said to Aisha: Which of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was most beloved to him? She said: Abu Bakr. I said: Then who? She said: Then Umar. I said: Then who? She said: Then Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah. I said: Then who? He said: Then she fell silent."
"4889","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah and Yazid narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Amr al-Laythi narrated to us, Abu Salama narrated to us, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray while I lay across in front of him in the house; when he wanted to pray witr, he would nudge me with his foot and say: Move aside."
"4890","Mujahid narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once sent sheep as a gift to the House, and garlanded them."
"4891","Mujahid narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Dhakwan, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Consult women about their marriages. They said: O Messenger of Allah, the virgin is shy? He said: Her silence is her consent."
"4892","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he wanted to sleep while junub, he would perform ablution as for prayer, and when he wanted to eat, he would wash his hands, then eat."
"4893","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like sweets and honey."
"4894","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aisha who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I know when you are angry with me and when you are pleased with me; when you are angry with me, you say: No, by the Lord of Ibrahim, and when you are pleased with me, you say: No, by the Lord of Muhammad. She said: Yes, by Allah, I abandon nothing but your name."
"4895","Abdullah ibn al-Rumi narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I know when you are pleased with me and when you are angry with me. She said: I said: How do you know that? He said: When you are pleased with me, you say: No, by the Lord of Muhammad, and when you are angry with me, you say: No, by the Lord of Ibrahim. I said: Yes, by Allah, I abandon nothing but your name."
"4896","Abdullah ibn al-Rumi narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aisha, that she and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe from a single vessel."
"4897","Abdullah ibn al-Rumi narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love sweets and honey; when he had prayed Asr, he would visit his wives and draw near to them. He entered upon Hafsa and stayed with her longer than he used to stay. I asked about that, and it was said to me: A woman of her people gave her a skin of honey, and she gave the Prophet a drink. I said: By Allah, we shall contrive against him. I mentioned that to Sawda, saying: When he enters upon you, he will draw near, so say to him: O Messenger of Allah, have you eaten maghafir? He will say to you: Hafsa gave me a drink of honey. So say to him: Its bees have fed on urfut. And I shall say that to him, and you, O Safiya, say it too. When he entered upon Sawda, Sawda said: By Allah, besides whom there is no god, I had meant to confront him with what you told me, while he was at the door, out of fear of you. When he drew near, she said: O Messenger of Allah, have you eaten maghafir? He said: No. I said: What is this smell? He said: Hafsa gave me a drink of honey. She said: I said: Its bees have fed on urfut. When he entered upon me, I said to him the same, then he entered upon Safiya, and she said the same to him. When he entered upon Hafsa, she said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I give you a drink? He said: I have no need for it. Sawda said: Glory be to Allah, we have deprived him. She said: I said: Be quiet."
"4898","Abdullah ibn al-Rumi narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me when I was six years old, and consummated with me when I was nine years old. We came to Medina and I was ill for a month, and my hair grew to earlobes. Umm Ruman came to me while I was on a swing, and shouted at me, so I came to her, not knowing what was wanted of me. She took my hand and stood me at the door, and I said: Heh, heh, until my breath settled. She took me into a house where there were women of the Ansar, and they said to me: Upon good and blessing, upon the best omen. They handed me to them, and they washed my head and prepared me, and nothing startled me but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they handed me to him."
"4899","Suwayd ibn Saeed narrated to us, Salih ibn Musa narrated to us, from Muawiya ibn Ishaq, from Aisha bint Talha, from Aisha, Mother of the Believers, who said: By Allah, I was in my house one day, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions in the courtyard, and a curtain between me and them, when Talha ibn Ubaydullah came. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man walking on the face of the earth having fulfilled his vow, let him look at Talha."
"4900","Suwayd ibn Saeed narrated to us, Salih ibn Musa narrated to us, from Muawiya ibn Ishaq, from Aisha bint Talha, from Aisha, Mother of the Believers, who said: By Allah, I was in my house one day, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the courtyard with his companions, and a curtain between me and them, when Abu Bakr came. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to look at one freed from the Fire, let him look at Abu Bakr; and the name his family called him was Abdullah ibn Uthman, but the name Atiq prevailed over him."
"4901","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Shabi, from Masruq who said: I asked Aisha about this verse concerning the vision. She said: I am the most knowledgeable of this umma about this, and I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that. He said: I saw Jibril. Then she said: Whoever claims that Muhammad saw his Lord has uttered a great lie against Allah."
"4902","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Ismail, from al-Shabi, from Masruq who said: I said to her, O mother - meaning Aisha - did Muhammad see his Lord? She said: My hair stood on end at what you said."
"4903","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Ismail, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aisha who said: He saw Jibril in his form twice."
"4904","Sahl ibn Zanjala al-Razi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: I asked al-Zuhri: Which of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought refuge from him? He said: Urwa informed me, from Aisha: That the daughter of al-Jawn al-Kilabiya, when she was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he drew near her, she said: I seek refuge in Allah from you. He said: You have sought refuge in a Mighty Refuge; join your family."
"4905","Abu Ubayda ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, Malik ibn Suayr ibn al-Khims narrated to us, al-Sari ibn Ismail narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Aisha who said: We used to place the siwak of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his purification water. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, you never leave the siwak. He said: Yes; if I were able for that to be from me at every paired prayer, I would do so."
"4906","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No wealth benefited us as the wealth of Abu Bakr benefited us."
"4907","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. Hushaym said: And the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"4908","Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muammar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian, and the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"4909","Abu al-Rabi al-Ataki narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter upon me while I was playing with toys, and sit with me looking at me for a long time, then stand."
"4910","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted ruqya for venomous stings."
"4911","Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed me, he said: Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yahya al-Qattan narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Muslim who said: Masruq said, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once did something and permitted it, and it reached him that some men refrained from it. So he stood and addressed and said: What is with men who know that I have done something and permitted it, yet refrain from it? By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of them about Allah and the most fearful of Him."
"4912","Suwayd ibn Saeed narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Tarif, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, that Aisha narrated to them that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast all of Shaban. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the most beloved month to you to fast is Shaban? He said: Allah writes the death of every soul in that year, so I love that my term comes to me while I am fasting."
"4913","Suwayd ibn Saeed narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Saeed, from Amra, from Aisha who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to observe itikaf, he would pray Fajr then enter his place of seclusion. When it was the morning of the twenty-first, he left after Fajr and entered the mosque and saw tents: the tent of Aisha, and she had sought his permission, and of Hafsa and Zaynab. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you intend righteousness by them? So he delayed his itikaf to Shawwal."
"4914","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from his father, from Masruq who said: Aisha said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about turning in prayer. He said: It is a snatching which Satan snatches from the prayer of the servant."
"4915","Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubayda narrated to us, Amr ibn Hani informed me, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Hand me my cloak. She handed it to him, and he went out and ascended the minbar, and the people gathered to him. He said: O people, Allah says: You shall command good and forbid evil before you suffer drought and seek rain and are not given rain. O people, Allah says: You shall command good and forbid evil before you supplicate and are not answered."
"4916","He said: I asked Abd al-Ala about the hadith of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and he said: This is a mistake. And he narrated to me with it, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from his father, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The siwak is purification for the mouth and pleasing to the Lord."
"4917","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, also al-Darawardi Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from his father, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The siwak is purification for the mouth and pleasing to the Lord."
"4918","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from a man, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning His saying: (And those who give what they give while their hearts fear that they will return to their Lord): O daughter of al-Siddiq - or O daughter of Abu Bakr - they are those who pray and fast while fearing that it will not be accepted from them, and give charity while fearing that it will not be accepted from them."
"4919","Amr ibn Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Ulatha narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sleeps after Asr and his mind is taken away, let him blame none but himself."
"4920","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha who said: Hamza ibn Amr al-Aslami asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, shall I fast while traveling? He said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"4921","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Saeed, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aisha, if I wished, mountains of gold would travel with me. An angel came to me whose waist-wrapper equals the Kaba, and said: Your Lord greets you with peace and says to you: If you wish, a prophet-servant, and if you wish, a prophet-king. He said: So I looked at Jibril. He said: He signaled to me to humble myself. He said: So I said: A prophet-servant. He said: After that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not eat reclining, saying: I eat as the servant eats, and I sit as the servant sits."
"4922","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to me, from his father, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the waiting period of Barira, when her husband parted from her, like that of a divorced woman."
"4923","Humayd ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ata narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu al-Zubayr, that Aisha, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking refuge in his prayer from the trial of the Masih al-Dajjal."
"4924","Musa ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abbas, from Abdullah al-Aslami, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a gazelle containing beads, and he divided it between the free and the slave. She said: And my father used to divide between the free and the slave."
"4925","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad Sajjada narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided Sura al-Baqara in two rakahs."
"4926","Muslim ibn Abi Muslim al-Jarmi narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha, Mother of the Believers, that it was mentioned to her that some people say: There is no ghusl except from seminal fluid. She said: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did that, and we bathed."
"4927","Muslim al-Jarmi narrated to us, Makhlad narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra who said: They discussed in a circle in which I was what obligates ghusl. Some said: When a man mingles, and some said: Until fluid is emitted. He said: So I said: I shall bring you knowledge of that. So I came to Aisha, Mother of the Believers, and said to her: O Mother of the Believers, I want to ask you about something, and I am shy to ask you about it. She said: Do not be shy to ask me about what you would ask your mother, for I am only your mother. I said: O mother, what obligates ghusl? She said: You have landed upon an expert: When he sits between her four parts and the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl has become obligatory."
"4928","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman al-Madani narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, and Saeed ibn al-Musayyib, and Alqama ibn Waqqas al-Laythi, and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba, from Aisha, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the people of the slander said to her what they said, so Allah declared her innocent of it - al-Zuhri said, and all of them narrated to me a portion of her hadith, some more retentive than others and more precise, and I retained from each man the hadith he narrated to me from Aisha, and part of their hadith confirms part - they claimed that Aisha said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted a journey, he would cast lots among his wives; whichever one's lot came out, he would go out with her. She said: So he cast lots among us in a campaign he undertook, and my lot came out, so I went out with him after the veil had been revealed. I would be carried in a howdah and set down in it. We traveled until, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had finished that campaign and turned back, and we drew near Medina, he announced departure one night. I stood when they announced departure and walked until I passed the army. When I had relieved myself, I came to my mount and felt my chest, and my necklace of onyx beads had broken. So I returned seeking my necklace, and seeking it detained me. Those who would mount me came, carried my howdah and mounted it upon my camel on which I rode, thinking I was in it - for women at that time were light, not heavy, nor covered with flesh; they ate only a morsel of food - so the people did not notice the weight of the howdah when they lifted and carried it, and I was a young girl. They sent the camel and marched. I found my necklace after the army had gone on. I came to their camp with no one in it, so I headed for my place where I had been, thinking they would miss me and return to me. While I sat in my place, my eyes overcame me and I slept. Safwan ibn al-Muattal al-Sulami then al-Dhakwani was behind the army; he reached my place in the morning, saw the black shape of a person and came to me - he used to see me before the veil - and I awoke at his istirja when he recognized me. I covered my face with my jilbab. By Allah, I did not speak a word, nor did I hear from him a word other than his istirja, until he made his camel kneel, trod its foreleg, and I rode it. He set out leading the mount with me until we reached the army while they halted at midday. Those who perished perished, and the one who took upon himself most of it was Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul. We came to Medina and I fell ill there for a month, while people spread the saying of the slanderers, and I sensed nothing of that. What troubled me in my illness was that I did not recognize from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the kindness I used to see from him when I fell ill; he would only enter, greet, then say: How is she? That troubled me, and I did not sense until I recovered. I went out with Umm Mistah bint Abi Ruhm toward al-Manasi, our place of relieving ourselves - we would go out only at night - and that was before we had taken privies near our houses; our affair was the affair of the early Arabs in the open or in seclusion. I and Umm Mistah bint Abi Ruhm walked, and she stumbled in her wrap and said: May Mistah perish. I said to her: What an evil thing you said; do you insult a man who witnessed Badr? She said: O dear, have you not heard what they said? She said: I said: What did they say? She informed me of the saying of the slanderers, and my sickness increased upon my sickness. When I returned to my house, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me and said: How is she? I said: Permit me to go to my parents. She said: I then wanted to verify the news from them. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted me, and I came to my parents. I said to my mother: What are people saying? She said: O daughter, take the matter lightly upon yourself; by Allah, seldom is there a beautiful woman with a man who loves her, having co-wives, except they multiply against her. She said: I said: Glory be to Allah, and people have spoken of this? I spent that night until morning with tears unceasing and no sleep. Then morning came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ali ibn Abi Talib and Usama ibn Zayd, when revelation delayed, consulting them about parting from his family. As for Usama ibn Zayd, he advised him with what he knew of his family's innocence and what he knew in himself of love for her. Usama said: Your wife, O Messenger of Allah, and by Allah we know only good. As for Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has not constrained you, and women besides her are many; ask the slave girl, she will tell you the truth. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Barira and said: O Barira, have you seen anything suspicious about her? Barira said: No, by He who sent you with the truth; I have not seen anything to criticize about her more than that she is a young girl who sleeps over the dough, so the household animal comes and eats it. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose that day and sought excuse from Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will excuse me from a man whose harm has reached my family? By Allah, by Allah, by Allah - three times - I have known only good about my family, and they have mentioned a man about whom I have known only good, and he would not enter upon my family except with me. Saad ibn Muadh stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I shall excuse you from him; if he is from Aws, we shall strike his neck, and if he is from our brothers Khazraj, command us and we shall carry out your command concerning him. Saad ibn Ubada stood - he was chief of Khazraj, previously a righteous man, but zeal carried him - and said: You have lied, by Allah, by Allah you shall not kill him, nor can you kill him. Usayd ibn Hudayr stood and said: You have lied, by Allah, by Allah we shall kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of hypocrites. So the two tribes, Aws and Khazraj, flared up until they nearly fought, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing upon the minbar. He said: So he descended and calmed them until they fell silent, and he fell silent. She said: I wept my day with tears unceasing and no sleep. My parents came to me in the morning, and I had wept two nights and a day until I thought weeping would split my liver. She said: While they sat with me and I wept, a woman of the Ansar sought permission, so I permitted her, and she sat weeping with me. While we were so, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and sat - he had not sat with me since what was said was said before, and a month had passed with nothing revealed to him concerning me. She said: He testified, then said: To proceed, O Aisha, such and such has reached me about you; if you are innocent, Allah will declare you innocent, and if you have committed, seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant confesses his sin then repents, Allah forgives him. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his speech, my tears ceased until I felt not a drop. I said to my father: Answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me concerning what he said. She said: He said: By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said to my mother: Answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me concerning what he said. She said: By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: I was a young girl not reading much of the Quran, so I said: By Allah, I have known that you heard what is said, and it has settled in your souls, and you believed it. If I say to you: I am innocent - and Allah knows I am innocent - you will not believe me in that, and if I confess to you something - and Allah knows I am innocent of it - you will believe me. By Allah, I find no example for me and you except Abu Yusuf when he said: (Patience is beautiful, and Allah is the Helper against what you describe). She said: Then I turned upon my bed, hoping Allah would declare me innocent, but by Allah I did not think revelation to be recited concerning me would descend, for I was too insignificant in myself for the Quran to be spoken concerning my affair; but I hoped the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would see in sleep a vision declaring me innocent. She said: By Allah, he had not left his seat, nor had anyone of the household gone out, until revelation descended upon him. He was seized by what used to seize him of heaviness, until sweat like pearls poured from him on a winter day. She said: When it was lifted from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he laughed, the first word he spoke was to say: O Aisha, praise Allah, for He has declared you innocent. My mother said to me: Stand to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: By Allah, I shall not stand to him, nor praise but Allah. And Allah revealed: (Those who brought the slander are a band among you) all the verses. When Allah revealed this concerning my innocence, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq - who used to spend upon Mistah ibn Uthatha for his kinship - said: By Allah, I shall never spend upon Mistah anything after what he said about Aisha. So Allah revealed this verse: (Let not the possessors of bounty and means among you swear not to give kinsfolk, the poor, and emigrants in Allah's path; let them pardon and overlook; do you not love that Allah forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful). Abu Bakr said: Yes, by Allah, I love that Allah forgive me. So he returned to Mistah what he used to spend upon him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had asked Zaynab bint Jahsh about my affair, saying: O Zaynab, what did you know and see? She said: O Messenger of Allah, I guard my hearing and sight; by Allah, I knew only good about her. Aisha said: She is the one who rivaled me, yet Allah protected her through piety."
"4929","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Rabia ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, and Yahya ibn Saeed, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, with the like of it."
"4930","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, and Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, with the like of it."
"4931","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Fulayh said: I heard some men of knowledge saying: The people of the slander were flogged the hadd, though we do not know that."
"4932","Hawthara ibn Ashras narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Urwa, from Aisha who said: People spoke of this affair and it spread among them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood as a preacher, and I was unaware of it. She said: I went out one night with Umm Mistah to relieve myself, and she stumbled and said: May Mistah perish. I said: Glory be to Allah, why do you insult your son, and he is among the early emigrants and witnessed Badr? She said: By Allah, I insult him only concerning you. I said: What is my affair? She informed me of the matter, and my need vanished and I found nothing of it, and I took fever. I came home, and my mother was below, and my father above the house praying. She embraced me and wept, and I wept, and Abu Bakr heard our weeping and said: What is with my daughter? My mother said: She heard that report. He said: Stay until we go with you in the morning to the Messenger of Allah. In the morning we went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with him was a woman of the Ansar; her presence did not prevent the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from speaking, and he said: O Aisha, if you have done wrong or erred, seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him. I said to my father: Speak. He said: With what shall I speak? I said to my mother: Speak. She said: With what shall I speak? So I praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: By Allah, if I say: I did, while Allah knows I did not, you will say: She has confessed; and if I say: I did not, while Allah knows I did not, you will say: She has lied. I find no example for me and you except what the righteous servant said - I forgot his name - so I said: Abu Yusuf: (Patience is beautiful, and Allah is the Helper against what you describe). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a Nubian slave girl and said: O so-and-so, what do you know of Aisha? She said: By Allah, I know no fault in Aisha except that she sleeps and the household animal enters and eats her dough and her mat. When she realized what he wanted, she said: By Allah, I know of Aisha only what the goldsmith knows of pure red gold. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the minbar and said: Advise me, O community of Muslims, concerning people who slander my family. By Allah, I have known only good about my family - and with whom do they slander them? By Allah, I have known only good about him, and he never entered my house except with me present, nor did I travel except with him. Saad ibn Muadh said: I think, O Messenger of Allah, that you strike their necks. Men of Khazraj stood and said: By Allah, had they been from your kin Aws, you would not have ordered striking their necks, until it nearly came to conflict between Aws and Khazraj. Revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Aisha said: He was not relieved until I saw joy between his eyes, and he said: Rejoice, O Aisha, for Allah has sent down your excuse. My parents said: Stand and kiss the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: I praise Allah, not you two. And he recited to them the Quran: (Those who brought the slander are a band among you; think it not evil for you, rather it is good for you; for each man among them what he earned of sin, and he who took upon himself most of it shall have a great punishment), (Had you, when you heard it, said: It is not for us to speak of this; glory be to You, this is a great slander). Among those who took upon themselves most of it were Hassan ibn Thabit, Mistah ibn Uthatha, and Hamna bint Jahsh; it was spoken in the presence of Abdullah ibn Ubayy, who heard it, spread it, and broadcast it. When Hassan ibn Thabit was insulted in Aisha's presence, she would say: Do not insult Hassan, for he used to defend the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then she would say: What punishment is greater than the loss of his eyes? And he about whom what was said was said: By Allah, I never uncovered a woman, and he was killed as a martyr in the path of Allah. Hassan ibn Thabit said, clearing himself: Chaste, weighed with a husband."
"4933","Hawthara narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Urwa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged those who said about Aisha what they said, eighty each: Hassan ibn Thabit, Mistah ibn Uthatha, and Hamna bint Jahsh."
"4934","Abu Yala and al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us, they said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abdullah al-Wasiti al-Tahhan narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Saad narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab al-Wasiti, Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, Saeed ibn al-Musayyib, Alqama ibn Waqqas, and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba narrated to me, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the people of the slander said about her what they said, Allah declared her innocent; and each narrated to me a portion of her hadith, and some were more retentive than others and more precise in narration, and I retained from each one the hadith he narrated from Aisha. Aisha said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to go on a journey, he would cast lots among his wives; whichever one's lot came out, he would take her out with him. Aisha said: So he cast lots among us in a campaign he undertook, and my lot came out therein, so I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after the veil had been revealed. I would be carried in a howdah and set down in it. We traveled until, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had finished that campaign, turned back and drew near Medina returning, he permitted us to depart. I stood when he permitted departure and walked until I passed the army. When I had relieved myself, I came to my mount and felt my chest, and my necklace of onyx beads had broken. So I returned seeking my necklace, and seeking it detained me. The group who used to mount me came, carried my howdah and mounted it upon my camel on which I rode, thinking I was in it - for women at that time were light, not covered with flesh, and we ate only a morsel of food - so the people did not notice the lightness of the howdah; they lifted and mounted it, and I was a young girl, so they sent and marched. I found my necklace after the army had gone on, and came to their dwellings with neither caller nor answerer therein. So I headed for my place where I had been, thinking they would miss me and return to me. While I sat in my place, my eye overcame me and I slept. Safwan ibn al-Muattal al-Sulami then al-Dhakwani was behind the army; he traveled by night and reached my place in the morning, saw the black shape of a sleeping person, and recognized me when he saw me - he used to see me before the veil - and I awoke at his istirja when he recognized me. I covered my face with my jilbab. By Allah, I did not speak a word, nor did I hear from him a word other than his istirja when he made his camel kneel, trod upon its foreleg, and I rose and rode it. He set out leading the mount with me until we reached the army while they had halted. She said: Those who perished perished, and the foremost who took upon himself most of it was Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul. Urwa said: I was informed that it was rumored and spoken of in his presence, and he affirmed, spread, and broadcast it. Ibrahim said, meaning he broadcast it. Urwa said: None of the slanderers was named except Mistah ibn Uthatha and Hamna bint Jahsh, among other people I have no knowledge of, except that they were a band, as Allah said; and most of that was said to be from Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul. Urwa said: Aisha disliked Hassan ibn Thabit to be insulted in her presence, saying: He is the one who said: And my honor. Aisha said: I came to Medina and fell ill when I arrived for a month, while people spread the saying of the slanderers, and I sensed nothing of that. What troubled me in my pain was that I did not recognize from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the kindness I used to see when I complained; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would only enter upon me saying: How is she? and leave. That is what troubled me, and I did not sense until I went out after recovering. I went out with Umm Mistah toward al-Manasi, and it was our place of relieving ourselves; our affair was the affair of the early Arabs in seclusion, before stools - we were harmed by taking privies at our houses. She said: I set out with Umm Mistah, daughter of Abi Ruhm ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf - her mother was daughter of Sakhr ibn Amir, maternal aunt of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and her son Mistah ibn Uthatha ibn Abbad ibn Abd al-Muttalib. I and Umm Mistah came toward my house when we had finished our affair, and Umm Mistah stumbled in her wrap and said: May Mistah perish. I said to her: What an evil thing you said; do you insult a man who witnessed Badr? She said: O dear, have you not heard what he said? I said: What did he say? So she informed me of the saying of the slanderers. She said: My sickness increased upon my sickness. When I returned to my house, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me and said: How is she? I said: Permit me to go to my parents. She said: I wanted to verify the news from them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted me, and I came to them. I said to my mother: O mother, what are people saying? She said: Take it lightly upon yourself; by Allah, seldom is there a beautiful woman with a husband who loves her, having co-wives, except they multiply against her. She said: I said: Glory be to Allah, have people spoken of this? She said: I wept that night until morning with tears unceasing and no sleep. She said: Then I awoke weeping. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ali ibn Abi Talib and Usama ibn Zayd, consulting them about parting from his family. As for Usama ibn Zayd, he advised the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with what he knew of his family's innocence and what he knew for them in himself. Usama ibn Zayd said: O Messenger of Allah, your wife, and we know only good. As for Ali, he said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has not constrained you regarding women, and women besides her are many; ask the slave girl, she will tell you the truth. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Barira and said: O Barira, have you seen anything suspicious? Barira said to him: By He who sent you with the truth, I have never seen concerning her anything to criticize more than that she is a young girl who sleeps over her family's dough, so the household animal comes and eats it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose that day and sought excuse from Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul while upon the minbar, saying: O community of Muslims, who will excuse me from a man whose harm concerning my family has reached me? By Allah, I have known only good about my family, and they mentioned a man of whom I knew only good, and he never entered upon my family except with me. Saad ibn Muadh, one of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, I shall excuse you from him; if he is from Aws, I shall strike his neck, and if he is from our brothers of Khazraj, command us and we shall do what you command us. A man of Khazraj stood - the mother of Hassan was his paternal cousin of his clan, and he was Saad ibn Ubada, chief of Khazraj, a righteous man, but zeal carried him - and said to Saad ibn Muadh: You have lied; by Allah you shall not kill him, nor can you kill him; had he been from your kin, you would not have wished him killed. Usayd ibn Hudayr, cousin of Saad ibn Muadh, stood and said to Saad ibn Ubada: You have lied; by Allah, we shall kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of hypocrites. She said: The two tribes, Aws and Khazraj, flared up until they nearly fought, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting upon the minbar. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept calming them until they fell silent, and he fell silent. She said: I wept all that day with tears unceasing and no sleep. She said: My parents came to me in the morning; I wept my day and night with tears unceasing and no sleep. She said: Until I thought weeping would split my liver. She said: While my parents sat with me and I wept, a woman of the Ansar sought permission upon me, so I permitted her, and she sat weeping with me. She said: While we were so, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, greeted, then sat. She said: He had not sat with me since what was said was said before, and a month had passed with nothing revealed to him concerning me. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) testified when he sat, then said: To proceed, O Aisha, such and such has reached me about you; if you are innocent, Allah will declare you innocent, and if you have committed a sin, seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant confesses and repents, Allah forgives him. She said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his speech, my tears ceased until I felt not a drop. I said to my father: Answer the Messenger of Allah for me concerning what he said. He said: By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: I said to my mother: Answer the Messenger of Allah for me concerning what he said. She said: By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: I said, a young girl not reading much of the Quran: By Allah, I have known, and you have heard, until it settled in your souls and you believed it. If I say to you: I am innocent, you will not believe me in that; and if I confess something, and Allah knows I am innocent of it, you will believe me. By Allah, I find no example for me nor you except Abu Yusuf when he says: (Patience is beautiful, and Allah is the Helper against what you describe). She said: I turned and lay upon my bed, and Allah knows then that I am innocent, and Allah will declare me innocent through my innocence; but by Allah, I did not think Allah would send down revelation concerning me, for my affair was too insignificant in myself for Allah to speak concerning me with a declaration; but I hoped the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would see in sleep a vision by which Allah would declare me innocent. She said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had not risen from his seat, nor had anyone of the household gone out, until Allah sent down upon him. He was seized by what used to seize him of heaviness, until sweat like pearls poured from him, on a winter day, from the weight of the Quran sent down upon him. She said: It was lifted from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he laughed, and the first word he spoke was to say: O Aisha, as for Allah, He has declared you innocent. She said: My mother said: Stand to him. I said: By Allah, I shall not stand to him, and I praise none but Allah. And Allah revealed: (Those who brought the slander are a band among you; think it not evil for you) the verses. When Allah sent down this concerning my innocence, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who spent upon Mistah ibn Uthatha for his kinship and poverty, said: By Allah, I shall never spend upon Mistah anything after what he said about Aisha. So Allah revealed: (Let not the possessors of bounty among you and means swear not to give kinsfolk) to His saying: (And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful). Abu Bakr said: Yes, by Allah, I love that Allah forgive me. So he returned to Mistah the spending he used to spend upon him. He said: By Allah, I shall never withdraw it from him. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had asked Zaynab bint Jahsh about my affair, saying to Zaynab: What did you know or see? She said: O Messenger of Allah, I guard my hearing and sight; by Allah, I knew only good. Aisha said: She is the one who used to rival me among the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), yet Allah protected her through piety, while her sister Hamna fought and perished among those who perished. Ibn Shihab said: This is what reached me of the hadith of this group."
"4935","Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab who said: And Aisha said: By Allah, the man about whom what was said was said says: Glory be to Allah! By Allah, I never uncovered a woman. She said: Then he was killed afterwards in the path of Allah."
"4936","Ahmad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Saad narrated to us, Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab who said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, Saeed ibn al-Musayyib, Alqama ibn Waqqas, and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba narrated to me, from Aisha, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the people of the slander said to her what they said, and Allah declared her innocent. He said: Each narrated to me a portion of her hadith, some more retentive than others and more precise in narration, and I retained from each man the hadith he narrated from Aisha, and part of their hadith confirms part, though some were more retentive than others. They said: Aisha said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted a journey, he would cast lots among his wives; whichever one's lot came out, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out with her. When it was the campaign of Banu al-Mustaliq, he cast lots among his women as he used to do, and my lot came out over them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took me out with him. She said: Women at that time ate only a morsel, not laden with flesh so as to grow heavy. When my camel was saddled for me and I sat in my howdah, then the people who would mount me would come, take me by the bottom of the howdah, lift it, place it upon the camel's back, tie it with its ropes, then take the camel's head and set out. She said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had finished that journey, he headed back until, near Medina, he halted, spent part of the night, then departure was announced among the people. The people departed, and I went out for some need, with a necklace of onyx of Zafar upon my neck. When I finished, it slipped from my neck without my knowing. When I returned to the mount, I sought it upon my neck and did not find it, while people had begun departing. So I returned to the place I had gone from and sought it until I found it. The people behind me who used to saddle my camel for me came, having finished its saddling, took the howdah thinking I was in it as I used to do, carried it and tied it upon the camel without doubting I was in it, then took the camel's head and set out with it. I returned to the camp with neither caller nor answerer therein; the people had gone. She said: I wrapped myself in my jilbab, then lay in my place, knowing that if I were missed, they would return to me. She said: By Allah, while I lay, Safwan ibn al-Muattal al-Sulami passed by me - he had stayed behind the camp for some need and not followed the people - saw my black shape, came until he stood over me - he used to see me before the veil was imposed - and when he saw me, he said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return; the wife of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - while I was wrapped in my garments - and said: What kept you behind, may Allah have mercy on you? She said: I did not speak to him. Then he brought the camel near, saying: Ride, and withdrew from me. She said: So I rode and he took the camel's head and set out swiftly seeking the people. By Allah, we did not catch the people, nor was I missed until we awoke and the people had halted. When they settled, the man appeared leading me, and the people of the slander said what they said, and the camp shook. By Allah, I knew nothing of that. Then we came to Medina and soon I fell ill with a severe illness; nothing of that reached me, though the report had reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and my parents, mentioning neither little nor much of it, except that I noticed that from him: when he entered upon me with my mother nursing me, he would say: How is she? adding nothing to that. She said: Until I found it in myself, and said: O Messenger of Allah, when I saw his coldness, if you would permit me, I would move to my mother and she would nurse me. He said: It is no harm upon you. She said: So I moved to my mother, knowing nothing of what had happened, until I recovered from my pain after more than twenty nights. We were an Arab people not taking these privies the non-Arabs take in our houses; we disdained and disliked them; we would only go to the salt marshes of Medina, and women would go out each night for their needs. I went out one night for some need, with Umm Mistah bint Abi Ruhm ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf - her mother was daughter of Sakhr ibn Amir ibn Kaab ibn Saad ibn Taym, maternal aunt of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq. She said: By Allah, as she walked with me, she stumbled in her wrap and said: May Mistah perish. She said: I said: Evil, by Allah, is what you said to a man of the emigrants who witnessed Badr. She said: Has the news not reached you, O daughter of Abu Bakr? She said: I said: What news? She informed me of what the people of the slander had said. She said: I said: Has this happened? She said: Yes, by Allah it has happened. She said: By Allah, I could not relieve my need and returned. By Allah, I kept weeping until I thought weeping would split my liver. She said: I said to my mother: May Allah forgive you; people speak what they speak, and you mention nothing of that? She said: O daughter, take the matter lightly; by Allah, seldom is there a beautiful woman with a man who loves her, having co-wives, except they and people multiply against her. Then he mentioned nearly the hadith of Salih ibn Kaysan in full, as Muhammad ibn Khalid narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Saad."
"4937","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father who said: My father said to me: Aisha said to him: O son of my sister, you have seen of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) honoring al-Abbas something wondrous. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be seized by pain in the side, very severe. She said: We would say: The kidney vein seized the Messenger of Allah, not recognizing the side pain. One day the side pain seized the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and became very severe until he fainted. We feared for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and people rushed to him. She said: We thought he had pleurisy, so we force-fed him medicine in the side of his mouth. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was relieved and awoke. She said: He knew we had force-fed him, finding the trace of the ladud, and said: Did you think Allah imposed it upon me? Allah would never impose it upon me. By He in whose Hand is my soul, none in the house shall remain except be force-fed except my uncle. Aisha said: I saw them that day being force-fed one by one. Aisha said: And whoever in the house that day was mentioned for merit. She said: All the men were force-fed. She said: Then, by Allah, the ladud reached the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we were force-fed, by Allah, woman by woman. She said: Until the ladud reached a woman among us. She said: By Allah, I am fasting. We said to her: What an evil thought, that we leave you while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has sworn. She said: So we force-fed her, by Allah, O son of my sister, though she was fasting. He said: Urwa said: By Allah, Abbas took the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the seventy of the Ansar came to him at al-Aqaba, took for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledges from them, and stipulated upon them - that in the dawn of Islam and its beginning, before anyone worshiped Allah openly."
"4938","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ishaq ibn al-Azraq narrated to us, Zakariya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Salama, from al-Bahi, from Urwa, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to remember Allah at all his times."
"4939","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father who said: I asked Aisha about ruqya for venom. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted ruqya for every venomous sting."
"4940","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yazid ibn al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, that he mentioned that Aisha narrated to him: When she menstruated, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say to her: O daughter of Abu Bakr, tighten your waist-wrapper. He would embrace her at night as Allah willed, and would say takbir for his prayer, and seldom slept at night, after Allah said: (Stand the night except a little)."
"4941","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aisha who said: Two prayers the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never left, secretly nor openly: two rakahs before Fajr, and two rakahs after Asr."
"4942","Ali ibn al-Jaad narrated to us, Zuhayr informed us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Mujahid, that al-Saib asked Aisha, saying: I have grown old and cannot pray except sitting; what do you think? She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - or the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is half of his prayer standing."
"4943","Ali ibn al-Jaad narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwa, from Aisha who said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would send them, then not avoid anything the one in ihram avoids."
"4944","Ali ibn al-Jaad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira informed me, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burda who said: We entered upon Aisha, and she brought out to us a coarse waist-wrapper of Yemeni make, and a cloak of those you call mulabbada. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died in these two garments."
"4945","Hudba narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, with its isnad, the like of it."
"4946","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, from Ikrima who said: I asked Aisha: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ever recite verse? She said: Sometimes when he entered his house he would say verses."
"4947","Muhammad ibn Abi Mashar narrated to us, my father Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amra bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aisha who said: A man sneezed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What shall I say, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Say: Praise be to Allah. The people said: What shall we say to him, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Say: May Allah have mercy on you. The man said: What shall I reply to them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Say: May Allah guide you and set right your state."
"4948","Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiya narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Yahya, from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, from Amra, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the briber and the bribed."
"4949","Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Yaqub ibn al-Walid al-Madani narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays twenty rakahs between Maghrib and Isha, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"4950","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha - if Allah wills, thus Abd al-Ala dictated to us - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cool the Zuhr prayer in intense heat."
"4951","Suwayd ibn Saeed narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Maymun, from Ata, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to outstrip the tireless striving one, let him refrain from sins."
"4952","Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Hudhali narrated to us, Ashath ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zubayd al-Ayami narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Saeed, from his father, from Abu Salama, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would incline the vessel for the cat, and it would drink from it, then he would perform ablution for prayer."
"4953","Abu Mamar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Habib, from Ibn Abi Husayn, from Ata, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no emigration after the conquest, but jihad and intention; and when you are mobilized, march forth."
"4954","Abu Mamar narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Nafi, freedman of the family of Zayd ibn al-Khattab, narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, he said: Amra said, Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Overlook the slips of people of standing. He said: So I attended Abu Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm judging by that."
"4955","Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Marwan narrated to us, from Razin al-Bakri, our freedwoman called Salma of Bakr ibn Wail narrated to us, that she heard Aisha saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: O Aisha, is there any morsel? I brought him a loaf, and he placed it upon his mouth and said: O Aisha, has anything of it entered my belly? Likewise is the kiss of the fasting person; breaking fast is only from what enters, not from what exits."
"4956","Harun ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, from Masruq, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I wept. He said: What makes you weep? I said: Fatima insulted me. He called Fatima and said: O Fatima, did you insult Aisha? She said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: O Fatima, do you not love whom I love? She said: Yes. And hate whom I hate? She said: Yes. He said: I love Aisha, so love her. Fatima said: I shall never say to Aisha anything that hurts her."
"4957","Abu Musa al-Hammal narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love sweets and honey."
"4958","Harun al-Hammal narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed Asr, he would visit his wives and draw near to them."
"4959","Abu Musa also narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha who said: The bed of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which we slept was of leather stuffed with fiber."
"4960","And with its isnad from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered in the year of the conquest from Kada, from upper Mecca, and entered for umra from Kuda. Urwa would enter from both together, mostly entering from Kada, the nearer of the two to his house."
"4961","And with its isnad from Aisha who said: It weighed heavily upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that any odor be found from him. Abu Yala said: Meaning the smell of garlic and onion."
"4962","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Awbad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Aisha, Mother of the Believers, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbors, one whose door faces my door, and the other whose door is distant from my door though nearer in wall; with which shall I begin? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Begin with the one whose door faces your door. Abd al-Malik said: He is Abu Imran al-Jawni."
"4963","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Awbad narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Babanus who said: I entered with two other men upon Aisha, Mother of the Believers, and a man among us said to her: O Mother of the Believers, what do you say about intercourse during menstruation? She said: What is intercourse? Is it menstruation? He said: Yes. She said: It is menstruation as Allah named it. She said: When that was the case, I would wrap my waist-wrapper, and for him was what is above the wrapper. She began narrating to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never passed my door a day without saying a word that delighted my eye. She said: One day he passed and did not speak to me, and passed the next day and did not speak to me, and passed the next day and did not speak to me, and passed the next day and did not speak to me. I said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is angry with me over something. She said: So I bound my head, made my face pale, cast a pillow facing the house door, and leaned upon it. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed, looked at me, and said: What is with you, O Aisha? She said: O Messenger of Allah, I complained and have a headache. He said, saying: Rather, alas my head. She said: I remained only a little until he was brought carried in a cloak. She said: So I nursed him, never having nursed a sick person nor seen a dead person. She said: He raised his head, so I took it and leaned it upon my chest. She said: Usama ibn Zayd entered with a moist arak siwak in his hand. She said: He glanced at it. She said: I thought he wanted it, so I took it, softened it with my mouth, and handed it to him. She said: He took it and raised it to his mouth. She said: His hand trembled and it fell from his hand. Then he turned his face to me until his mouth was at my mouth; a cold drop flowed from his mouth, my skin shivered from it, and the scent of musk rose in my face. His head inclined, and I thought he had fainted. She said: I took him, laid him upon the bed, and covered his face. She said: My father Abu Bakr entered and said: How do you see him? I said: He has fainted. He drew near, uncovered his face, and said: O fainting, how unlike fainting this is. Then he uncovered his face and recognized death, saying: To Allah we belong and to Him we return. Then he wept. I said: For Allah's sake, the cessation of revelation and Jibril entering my house. Then he placed his hands upon his temples and his mouth upon his forehead, and wept until his tears flowed upon the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he covered his face and went out to the people weeping, saying: O community of Muslims, does any among you have a covenant about the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: No. Then he turned to Umar and said: O Umar, do you have a covenant about the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: No. He said: By He besides whom there is no god, he has tasted death; and he said to them: I am dead and you are dead. The people clamored and wept bitterly. Then they left him to his household. Ali ibn Abi Talib washed him, with Usama ibn Zayd pouring water over him. Ali said: I did not forget anything of him I had not washed except it was turned for me until I saw another and washed him without seeing another, until I finished him. Then they shrouded him in a red Yemeni cloak and two wraps that had been used then washed. Then he was laid upon the bed, permission given to people, and they entered upon him group by group praying over him without an imam, until none remained in Medina, free nor slave, except prayed over him. Then they disputed about his burial, where he should be buried. Some said: By the staff he held in his hand, beneath his minbar. Some said: In al-Baqi, where he buried his dead. They said: We shall not do that, lest a servant or slave girl of one of you angered by his master seek refuge at his grave as a practice. Their view settled that he be buried in his house beneath his bed where his soul was taken. When Abu Bakr died, he was buried with him. When death came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, he counseled, saying: When I die, carry me to the door of Aisha's house and say to her: This is Umar ibn al-Khattab greeting you with peace, saying: Shall I enter or go out? He said: She was silent a while, then said: Admit him and bury him with him; Abu Bakr at his right and Umar at his left. She said: When Umar was buried, I took the jilbab and wrapped myself in it. He said: It was said to her: What is with you and the jilbab? She said: This was my husband, and this was my father; when Umar was buried, I wrapped myself."
"4964","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha who said: Juwayriya came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I fell in the share of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, or a cousin of his, and I contracted for my freedom. So I have come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his help for my contract. He said: Is there something better than that: I pay your contract and marry you? She said: Yes. He said: I have done so."
"4965","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who divorced his wife irrevocably, meaning thrice, then she married a man who divorced her before consummating with her; does she return to the first? He said: No, until he tastes of her sweetness what her companion tasted."
"4966","Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariya narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Saeed, from al-Qasim, from Aisha, the like of it."
"4967","Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariya narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Saeed, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, the like of it."
"4968","Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythama Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abu Mamar, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque with three hundred sixty idols around the Kaba, and began striking them with a stick in his hand, saying: Truth has come and falsehood has vanished; falsehood is ever vanishing."
"4969","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abu Mamar, from Abdullah who said: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah into two halves, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bear witness."
"4970","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, Abd al-Karim al-Jazari narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam, from Abdullah ibn Maqil who said: I entered with my father upon Abdullah, and he said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Regret is repentance? He said: Yes."
"4971","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave when (By those sent forth in succession) was revealed upon him. I took it from his mouth while his mouth was moist. I do not know with which he sealed: (In what report after it will they believe), or (When it is said to them: Bow, they do not bow). A snake outran us and entered its hole. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You were protected from its evil, and it was protected from your evil."
"4972","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wail who said: Abdullah said: We used to greet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he would return it to us, meaning in prayer. When we came from the land of Abyssinia, I greeted him and he did not return it to me. I was seized by distress far and near. I sat until, when he finished prayer, I said to him: You used to return it to us. He said: Allah brings about what He wills, and He has brought about in His decree that you shall not speak in prayer."
"4973","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, Mughira narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid who said: I saw Abdullah ibn Masud stone the Aqaba pillar from the valley bottom, saying: This, by He besides whom there is no god, is the station of him upon whom Sura al-Baqara was revealed."
"4974","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughira, from Shibak, from Ibrahim, from Hunayy ibn Nuwayra, from Alqama, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most restrained of people in killing are the people of faith."
"4975","Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shuba, from Mughira, from Shibak, from Ibrahim, from Hunayy ibn Nuwayra, from Alqama, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The most restrained of people in killing are the people of faith."
"4976","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam began strange and shall return as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers. It was said: Who are the strangers? He said: Those who detach from tribes."
"4977","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow up between Hajj and Umra, for they remove poverty and sins as the bellows remove dross of iron, gold, and silver; and the accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise."
"4978","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun rises as it rises between the two horns of Satan. He said: So we were forbidden to pray at sunrise, at sunset, and at midday."
"4979","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a need, and he said: Bring me something to clean myself with, and do not bring me a bone nor dung."
"4980","Abu Nasr Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Tammar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Amr ibn Maymun, that Ibn Masud narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall be in the Fire a people as long as Allah wills, then Allah shall mercy them and bring them out, and they shall be in the lowest Paradise. They shall bathe in the River of Life, and the people of Paradise shall call them the Hell-dwellers. If one of them were to host the people of the world, he would feed, water, clothe, and furnish them - he said, and I think he said - and marry them, without diminishing what is with him."
"4981","Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from Ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last to enter Paradise is a man walking upon the Bridge once, stumbling once, scorched by the Fire once. When he turns to it, he says: Praise be to Allah who saved me from you; Allah has given me something He gave none of the first nor the last. A tree is raised for him, and he says: O Lord, bring me near this tree to shade in its shade and drink of its water. Allah says: O son of Adam, perhaps if I bring you near it, you will ask Me for other than it. He pledges not to ask Him, while his Lord knows he shall ask other than it, for he sees what he cannot bear. Allah brings him near it, and he shades in its shade and drinks of its water. Then another tree finer than that tree is raised for him, and he says: O Lord, bring me near this tree to shade in its shade and drink of its water. Allah says: O son of Adam, did you not pledge not to ask Me for other than it? He says: Yes, O Lord, but this tree - I shall ask You for nothing else. He pledges not to ask Him, while his Lord knows he shall ask other than it, and his Lord excuses him, for he sees what he cannot bear. Allah brings him near it, and he shades in its shade and drinks of its water. Then a tree at the gate of Paradise, finer than the first two trees, is raised for him, and he says: O Lord, bring me near this tree to shade in its shade and drink of its water. Allah says: O son of Adam, did you not pledge not to ask Me for other than it? He says: O Lord, bring me near this tree to shade in its shade and drink of its water. Allah says to him: Perhaps if I bring you near it, you will ask Me for other than it. He pledges not to ask Him for other than it, while his Lord knows he shall ask other than it, and his Lord excuses him, for he sees what he cannot bear. He brings him near it, and he hears the voices of the people of Paradise, saying: O Lord, admit me to Paradise. Allah says: Would it please you that I give you the world and its like with it? He says: O Lord, do You mock me while You are Lord of the worlds? He said: I do not mock you, but I am Able over what I will."
"4982","Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Cursed is the eater of usury, its giver, its two witnesses, and its scribe. And he said: Whenever adultery and usury appear among a people, they bring upon themselves Allah's punishment."
"4983","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The disbeliever shall be bridled by sweat on the Day of Resurrection, saying: Relieve me though to the Fire."
"4984","Ahmad ibn Hatim narrated to us, Khalaf, meaning Ibn Khalifa, narrated to us, from Humayd, meaning al-Araj, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah spoke to Musa while he wore a woolen outer garment, a woolen cloak, woolen trousers, a woolen cap, and his sandals of undressed donkey hide."
"4985","Abu Mamar Ismail al-Hudhali narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that al-Ashath ibn Qays bought slaves from the slaves of the emirate and they differed over the price. Ibn Masud said: I sold to you for twenty thousand, while al-Ashath said: I bought from you for ten thousand. Abdullah said: If you wish, I shall narrate a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah? He said: Give it. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When the two sellers differ with no proof between them, the word is the seller's, or they annul the sale. He said: Then I annul the sale."
"4986","Al-Mualla ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Zirr, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: I was a sturdy boy herding sheep for Uqba ibn Abi Muayt. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with Abu Bakr with him, saying: O boy, have you any milk? I said: Yes, but I am entrusted. He said: Bring me a sheep untouched by the ram. I brought him a young goat, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held it, then rubbed the udder and supplicated until it let down milk. Abu Bakr came with a rock hollow, and he milked into it. Then he said to Abu Bakr: Drink. Abu Bakr drank, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank after him. Then he said to the udder: Contract. It contracted and returned as it was. He said: Then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) afterwards and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me from this speech, or from this Quran. He wiped my head and said: You are a taught boy. He said: I took from his mouth seventy suras no human disputed with me."
"4987","Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifa narrated to us, from Humayd al-Araj, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: When (Who is it that lends Allah a good loan) was revealed, Abu al-Dahdah said: O Messenger of Allah, does Allah want a loan from us? He said: Yes, O Abu al-Dahdah. He said: Show me your hand. He gave him his hand. He said: I have lent my Lord my garden, containing six hundred palms. He walked until he reached the garden, with Umm al-Dahdah and his children in it, and called: O Umm al-Dahdah. She said: At your service. He said: Go out, for I have lent it to my Lord."
"4988","Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Hafs narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Ubayda, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Odd, loving the odd; so pray witr, O people of the Quran. A Bedouin said: What do you say, O Messenger of Allah? He said: It is not for you nor your companions."
"4989","Uthman narrated to us, Abu Hafs narrated to us, from al-Amash and Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Fighting the believer is disbelief, and insulting him is wickedness."
"4990","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your permission is to lift the veil and hear my private speech until I forbid you. He said: It reached me that it is confidences."
"4991","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdur Rahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he forbade going out to intercept (incoming trade caravans before they reach the market)."
"4992","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, Abu Amr al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reviling a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."
"4993","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed the spoils of Hunayn at al-Ji'irranah, and the people crowded around him, so he said: A servant among the servants of Allah, Allah sent him to his people, but they denied him, beat him and wounded his face. Abdullah said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the saddle, saying like this: My Lord, forgive my people, for they do not know. And Abu Sa'id al-Qawariri placed his thumb on his forehead, as if wiping something away."
"4994","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Jibril at the Lote Tree, having six hundred wings, with multicolored pearls and rubies scattering from his feathers."
"4995","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan: from his hamz, his nafkh and his nafth. He said: His hamz is madness, his nafth is poetry, and his nafkh is arrogance."
"4996","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The superiority of a man's prayer in congregation over his praying alone is twenty-odd degrees."
"4997","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Harun ibn Antarah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, and Alqamah, that they both said: We prayed with Ibn Mas'ud in his house, one of us on his right and the other on his left, and he said: This is how we prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4998","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: A black slave joined the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he died, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of it, so he said: See whether he left anything? They said: Two dinars. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two brands (of Fire)."
"4999","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My example and the example of this world is only like a rider who rests in the shade of a tree on a hot day, then departs and leaves it."
"5000","Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Murrah al-Hamdani, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan has a prompting, and the angel has a prompting. As for the prompting of Satan, it is a promise of evil and denial of the truth; and as for the prompting of the angel, it is a promise of good and affirmation of the truth. So whoever finds that, let him praise Allah, and whoever finds the other, let him seek refuge from Satan. Then he recited: Satan promises you poverty, to the end of the verse."
"5001","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Mu'arriq al-Ijli, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The congregational prayer exceeds a man's prayer alone by twenty-odd parts."
"5002","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir [the chain stops here, the text is truncated in this copy]."
"5003","And with the same chain: and from Mujahid, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah who said: While we were in Masjid al-Khayf on the night of Arafah, we heard the sound of a snake, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill it. It entered into a crack of its hole, so a palm frond was brought and fire was kindled in it, then we tore open part of the hole but did not find it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave it, for Allah has protected it from your harm, as He protected you from its harm."
"5004","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you doubts, let him seek what is most correct, and let him prostrate two prostrations."
"5005","Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the practices of guidance: prayer in the mosque in which the call to prayer is made."
"5006","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Sulayman ibn Atiq narrated to me, from Talq ibn Habib, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Shall I not tell you: ruined are the over-strict. Shall I not tell you: ruined are the over-strict. Shall I not tell you: ruined are the over-strict."
"5007","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abidah, from Abdullah, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept he would say: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You gather Your servants, and he would place his hand under his cheek."
"5008","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: They used to recite behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer, so he said: You have confused the Qur'an for me."
"5009","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Atiq, from Talq ibn Habib, from al-Ahnaf, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ruined are the over-strict, three times."
"5010","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah who said: We were with Abdullah, and Ziyad ibn Hudayr was with us, then Khabbab came in to us and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, do all of these recite as you recite? He said: If you wish, I will command one of them to recite to you. Then he said to me: Recite. Ibn Hudayr said to him: You command him to recite, yet he is not the best reciter among us? He said: If you wish, I will tell you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to your people and his people. So I recited to him fifty verses from Maryam, and Khabbab said: Enough."
"5011","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani informed me, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mill of Islam will turn after thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven years; if they perish, then the path of those who perished, and if they remain, their religion will remain for them for seventy years."
"5012","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah who said: We traveled one night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we said: O Messenger of Allah, if only we could touch the ground and sleep, while our mounts graze? He said: Then who will guard us? He said: So I said: I will. He said: Then my eyes overcame me, and nothing woke us except that the sun had risen, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not wake except at our talking. He said: So he commanded Bilal, who called the adhan, then he stood and prayed with us."
"5013","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Kaysan narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had informed me, from his father, from Ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the closest of people to me on the Day of Resurrection are those who send the most blessings upon me."
"5014","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sharik, from Uthman ibn Abi Zar'ah, from Abu Sadiq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise has eight gates: seven closed, and one gate open for repentance until the sun rises from its direction."
"5015","Abu Abdillah al-Muqaddami narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, that the companions of Ibn Mas'ud were bitten by the cold, and they felt shy to come in cloaks and outer garments, so he missed them, and it was said to him: Their situation is such and such, so Abu Abd al-Rahman awoke in an outer cloak, and they said: Ibn Mas'ud has awoken in his cloak. Then the second day came, then the third day came, and when they saw him in the cloak, they came together in their garments, and he recognized faces he had missed, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No one will enter Paradise in whose heart is the weight of a mustard seed of arrogance, or he said: an atom of arrogance."
"5016","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydillah, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the evening he would say: We have entered the evening, and the dominion belongs to Allah, and praise belongs to Allah; there is no god but Allah alone with no partner. O Allah, I ask You for the good of this night and the good of what is in it, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what is in it. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, old age, the evil of pride, the trial of this world, and the punishment of the grave."
"5017","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Mas'udi informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah, from his father Abdullah: That two men used to worship Allah and asked Allah to cause them both to die together; so they both died together and were buried. Abdullah said: If I had been there, I would have shown you their graves by the description the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described to us."
"5018","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Salam narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Regarding thirty cattle, a tabi' or tabi'ah (a one-year-old calf) is due, and regarding forty, a musinnah (a two-year-old cow)."
"5019","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ali ibn Salih, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray, and when he prostrated, al-Hasan and al-Husayn would jump onto his back, and when they wanted to stop them, he gestured to them to leave them alone, and when he finished the prayer, he placed them in his lap. He said: Whoever loves me, let him love these two."
"5020","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, regarding His saying: The heart did not deny what it saw, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Jibril in two garments of Rafraf (green brocade), filling what is between the heaven and the earth."
"5021","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibrahim who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abdullah: Recite to me. He said: Shall I recite to you, when it was revealed to you? He said: I love to hear it from other than myself. He said: So he recited to him from the beginning of Surat al-Nisa up to His saying: How will it be when We bring a witness from every nation and bring you as a witness over these, and he wept."
"5022","Mis'ar said: Ma'n narrated to me, from Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from his father, from Ibn Mas'ud who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A witness over them as long as I am among them, or he said: as long as I was among them; Mis'ar doubted."
"5023","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: My Lord, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants."
"5024","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Mis'ar who said: Ma'n ibn Abd al-Rahman brought out a book to me, and swore upon it that it was his father's handwriting, and in it was: Abdullah said: By the One besides whom there is no god, I have not seen anyone more severe against the over-strict than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor have I seen anyone more severe against them after him than Abu Bakr, and I think Umar was the most fearful of the people of the earth concerning them, or for them."
"5025","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas who said: Abdullah said: I have seen us, and none stayed behind from prayer except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known, or a sick person; indeed the sick person would walk between two men until he came to prayer. And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the practices of guidance, and among the practices of guidance is prayer in the mosque in which the call to prayer is made."
"5026","Mus'ab ibn Abdillah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah, that Ibn Mas'ud said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among nearly thirty men, among whom there was none but a Qurayshi; by Allah, I never saw the surface of men's faces more handsome than their faces that day. He said: Then they mentioned women, and talked about them, and he talked with them, until I wished he would fall silent. Then I came to him, and he bore witness, then said: To proceed, O assembly of Quraysh, you are the people of this matter as long as you obey Allah; but when you disobey Him, He will send upon you one who will strip you as this stick is stripped - for a stick in his hand - then he stripped his stick, and it was white and smooth."
"5027","Salih ibn Harb Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Sallam ibn Abi Khubzah narrated to us, Asim ibn Abi al-Najud narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog that is not a livestock dog or a hunting dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."
"5028","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Sulayman Abu Dawud narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a donkey called Ufayr."
"5029","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Aban ibn Taghlib narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, You have no partner, here I am; indeed praise and blessing belong to You."
"5030","Muhammad narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Bakr narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn the Qur'an, and learn knowledge and teach it to people, and learn the laws of inheritance and teach them to people, for I am a man who will be taken, and knowledge will be taken away, until two men differ over an inheritance law and find no one to inform them."
"5031","Muhammad narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Yazid, meaning Abu Ma'shar, narrated to us, Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month, supplicating against Usayyah and Dhakwan; then when he prevailed over them, he left qunut."
"5032","Muhammad narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasir, from Qays, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever lends a Muslim man a dirham twice, it will be for him like the reward of giving both in charity once."
"5033","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq who said: We were sitting with Abdullah after Maghrib while he was teaching us the Qur'an, when a man asked him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did you ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) how many caliphs will rule this nation? Ibn Mas'ud said: No one has asked me about it since I came to Iraq before you. He said: Yes, I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Twelve, like the chiefs of the Children of Israel."
"5034","Shayban narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abu Wa'il who said: We were sitting waiting for Ibn Mas'ud to come out to us, when Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah came to us, so we said: Sit. He said: Until I enter upon your companion; if he comes out, otherwise I will return to you. He said: So he entered upon him, and they both came out together, and Ibn Mas'ud said: I am informed of your gathering - or your place - and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except dislike of boring you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to choose the right time to exhort us on certain days, fearing weariness for us."
"5035","Shayban narrated to us, Ikrimah, meaning al-Azdi, narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Ibn Mas'ud who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muhajirun, the Ansar, the freed ones of Quraysh, and the freed ones of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."
"5036","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ghuniyyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah: That he was asked: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) deliver the sermon standing? He said: So he said: Yes, then he recited: And they left you standing."
"5037","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Abdullah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Salim al-Aftas, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man of the Children of Israel saw his brother committing a sin, he forbade him by way of excuse, but the next day what he saw of him did not prevent him from being his eating companion, his associate and his drinking companion. When Allah saw that of them, He struck the hearts of some of them upon others, and cursed them upon the tongue of their Prophet Dawud and Isa son of Maryam: That was because they disobeyed and transgressed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, you must command good, and you must forbid evil, and you must seize the hand of the wrongdoer, and you must bend him to the truth completely, or Allah will surely strike the hearts of some of you upon others, and will surely curse you as He cursed them."
"5038","Hudbah ibn Khalid and Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was brought al-Buraq, and I rode it behind Jibra'il, and we traveled; whenever it came to a mountain its feet rose, and when it descended its hands rose. So we traveled through a dark, foul land, and came out to a spacious, pleasant land. I said: O Jibra'il, we were traveling through a dark, foul land, and we have come out to a spacious, pleasant land. He said: That was the land of the Fire, and this is the land of Paradise. Then we came upon a man standing praying. He said: So he said: Who is this with you, O Jibra'il? He said: This is your brother Muhammad. So he welcomed me and supplicated for blessing for me. He said: Ask ease for your nation. He said: I said: Who is this, O Jibra'il? He said: This is your brother Isa. He said: Then we traveled, and came upon a man, who said: Who is with you, O Jibra'il? He said: This is your brother Muhammad. He said: So he welcomed me and supplicated for blessing for me. He said: Ask ease for your nation. He said: I said: Who is this, O Jibra'il? He said: This is your brother Musa. He said: Then we traveled, and saw lamps and light, and I said: What is this, O Jibra'il? He said: This is the tree of your father Ibrahim; will you approach it? He said: So I said: Yes, and we approached it, and he welcomed me and supplicated for blessing for me. Then we went on until we came to Bayt al-Maqdis, and the prophets were presented to me, those whom Allah named and those whom He did not name, and I prayed with them, except these three men: Musa, Isa and Ibrahim."
"5039","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah who said: A man of the people of al-Suffah died, and they found two dinars in his wrap, and that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Two brands."
"5040","Nu'aym ibn Haysam narrated to us, Khalid, meaning al-Wasiti, narrated to us, from Yahya al-Jabbar, from Abu Majidah, from Ibn Mas'ud who said: We asked our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about walking with the funeral, and he said: At less than a trot; if it is good, it is hastened to it, and if it is otherwise, then away with the people of the Fire. The funeral is followed, and does not follow; whoever goes ahead of it is not of it."
"5041","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar, and they did not raise their hands except at the opening of prayer. Muhammad said: They did not raise their hands after the first takbir."
"5042","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Alqamah who said: Ibn Mas'ud said: Shall I not pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: So he prayed with them, and raised his hand only once."
"5043","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Zaynab, from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah who said: I was praying with my left hand placed over my right, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and took my right hand and placed it over my left."
"5044","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi', from his father, from Abdullah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Usury, however much it be, its end turns to little."
"5045","Bishr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Ibn Mas'ud who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut only for a month, supplicating therein against a clan of the clans of Banu Sulaym; they were Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger, then he did not perform qunut after that."
"5046","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The idolaters detained the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Asr prayer until the sun yellowed - or reddened - so he said: They distracted us from the middle prayer; may Allah fill their bellies and their graves with fire, or: may Allah stuff their bellies and their graves with fire."
"5047","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Abdillah ibn Hubayrah, from Hanash al-San'ani, from Abdullah, that he recited in the ear of an afflicted man, who recovered, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What did you recite in his ear? He said: I recited: Did you think We created you in vain, until the end of the surah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a certain man recited it over a mountain, it would move."
"5048","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Abu Fazarah, from Abu Zayd, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution with nabidh (date infusion)."
"5049","Abdullah ibn Awn al-Kharraz narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Aban ibn Ishaq, from al-Sabbah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Hazim, from Murrah al-Hamdani, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be truly modest before Allah: let him guard the head and what it contains, let him guard the belly and what it holds, let him remember death and decay, and whoever desires the Hereafter leaves the adornment of this world; whoever does that has been truly modest before Allah."
"5050","Kamil ibn Talhah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that they said: O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your nation whom you have not seen? He said: Radiant with white marks, piebald from the traces of purification."
"5051","Sa'id ibn Ash'ath narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan informed me, Asim, meaning Ibn Bahdalah, narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: I cannot count how often I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in the two rak'ahs before Fajr prayer and in the two rak'ahs after Maghrib: Say, O disbelievers, and Say, He is Allah, One."
"5052","Sa'id ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid ibn Ma'dan informed me, Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in witr: in the first rak'ah, Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High; in the second, Say, O disbelievers; and in the third, Say, He is Allah, One."
"5053","And with his chain, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of the cheeks of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, to his right; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, to his left."
"5054","Sa'id ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, al-Haysam ibn al-Shaddakh al-Abdi informed me, from al-A'mash narrating from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: I am amazed at people abandoning my recitation and taking the recitation of Zayd, while I took seventy surahs from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Zayd ibn Thabit was a boy with a forelock, coming and going in Madinah."
"5055","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abdillah ibn Amr al-Awdi, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you who is forbidden to the Fire, or for whom the Fire is forbidden? For every gentle, close, easy person."
"5056","Abu Talib Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Abu Wasil, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the muhallil and the one for whom tahleel is done."
"5057","Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Shayban, from Firas, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man entered Paradise who had done no good; he said to his family when death came to him: When I die, burn me, then grind me, then scatter half of me on land and half of me in the sea. So He commanded the sea and the land and they gathered him. He said: What carried you to do what you did? He said: Fear of You. So He forgave him for that."
"5058","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, a similar hadith, and the man was a grave-robber, so he was forgiven for his fear."
"5059","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: Two men disputed over a surah; one said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to recite it, and the other said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to recite it. They came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was informed of that. He said: His face changed, and he said: Recite as you were taught. He mentioned some speech therein, then said: Those before you perished only by their differing over their prophets. He said: Then each man of us stood, reciting not according to the recitation of his companion."
"5060","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, Asim ibn Abi al-Najud narrated to us, from Zirr, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed with Abu Bakr and Umar while Abdullah was praying and began Surat al-Nisa, reciting it fully, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd. Then he sat, then asked, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying: Ask, you will be given. He said, among what he asked: O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, bliss that does not end, and the companionship of our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the highest Garden of Eternity. Then Umar came to give him glad tidings of it, but found Abu Bakr coming out, having preceded him, and said: If you did, you are indeed foremost in good."
"5061","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: I was praying in the mosque when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered with Abu Bakr and Umar, so I recited Surat al-Nisa at length and read it; when I finished I sat, and began with praise of Allah Almighty and blessing upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then supplicated for myself, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask, you will be given; ask, you will be given. Then he said: Whoever loves to recite the Qur'an fresh, let him recite it as Ibn Umm Abd recites it. He said: Then I returned to my home, and Abu Bakr came to me and said: Do you remember any of what you were supplicating? He said: I said: Yes: O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, bliss that does not end, and the companionship of our Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the highest Garden of Eternity. He said: Then Umar also came to me and gave me glad tidings."
"5062","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: And Amr ibn Abi Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, informed me, from a man of the family of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is easy, gentle and close, Allah forbids him to the Fire."
"5063","Hajjaj ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated to me, Zam'ah narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah informed me, from Ibn Mas'ud: That he performed tamattu' of Hajj with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5064","Hajjaj ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to me, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tonight I spent reciting to the jinn, companions at al-Hajun."
"5065","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have mercy on those on earth, and He who is in heaven will have mercy on you."
"5066","Suwayd ibn Sa'id and Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abdillah narrated to us, they said: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from Alqamah, from Ibn Mas'ud who said: When this verse was revealed: There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted, when they fear Allah, to the end of the verse, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was said to me: You are of them. And this is the wording of Abd al-Ghaffar."
"5067","Suwayd ibn Sa'id and Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, they said: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one will enter Paradise in whose heart is the weight of a mustard grain of arrogance, nor will the Fire touch one in whose heart is the weight of a grain of faith."
"5068","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one will enter Paradise in whose heart is the weight of a mustard grain of arrogance, nor will the Fire touch one in whose heart is the weight of a mustard grain of faith."
"5069","Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A'mash who said: I heard Ibn Yusuf, while he was on the pulpit, say: Arrange the Qur'an as Jibril arranged it: the surah in which the cow is mentioned, the surah in which the family of Imran is mentioned, the surah in which women are mentioned. Al-A'mash said: So I met Ibrahim and informed him, and he reviled him. Then Ibrahim said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid narrated to me that he was with Abdullah ibn Mas'ud when he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah; he went to the bottom of the valley and stoned it from the belly of the valley with seven pebbles, saying takbir with each pebble. I said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, people stone it from above it. So Ibn Mas'ud said: This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the station of the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed."
"5070","Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: I came to Hims, and some people there said to me: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, recite to us. So I recited Surat Yusuf. A man said to me: It was not revealed like this. I said to him: Woe to you, by Allah I recited it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: You have done well. He said: While I was arguing with him, I smelled wine from him, so I said to him: Do you drink filth and deny the Qur'an? Of course, you shall not leave until I flog you the prescribed punishment. So I flogged him the punishment."
"5071","Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Ubaydah al-Salmani, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite to us. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I recite to you when the Qur'an was revealed to you? He said: I love to hear it from other than myself. So I recited Surat al-Nisa to him, until when I reached: How will it be when We bring a witness from every nation and bring you as a witness over these, he nudged me, and I looked at him, and his eyes were flowing - (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5072","Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abdullah who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the moon split into two halves; one half was behind the mountain and one half below it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bear witness."
"5073","Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, will we be taken to account for what we did in ignorance? He said: Whoever does good in Islam will not be taken for what he did in ignorance, but whoever does evil in Islam will be taken for the first and the last."
"5074","Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) telling of a prophet among the prophets, whom his people struck until they bloodied his face, and he kept wiping the blood from his face, saying: My Lord, forgive my people, for they do not know."
"5075","Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Take suhur, for in suhur there is blessing."
"5076","Asim ibn al-Nadr ibn al-Muntashir al-Ahwal narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi' narrate, from al-Qasim ibn Hassan, from his uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dislike ten traits: yellowness - meaning perfume with saffron - dragging the lower garment, wearing a gold ring, plucking grey hair, playing with dice, displaying adornment in improper place, ruqyah except with the Mu'awwidhat, hanging amulets, withdrawing water at its time from its place, and corrupting the child without making him unlawful."
"5077","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Awsajah ibn al-Rammah, from Abdillah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, You have made my creation good, so make my character good."
"5078","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-odd degrees."
"5079","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from Satan, from his hamz, his nafth and his nafkh. His hamz is madness, his nafkh is poetry, and his nafth is arrogance."
"5080","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father and Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, they said: Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no envy except in two cases: a man to whom Allah gave wealth and empowered him to spend it in truth, and a man to whom Allah gave wisdom, so he judges by it and teaches it."
"5081","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ayyub ibn Hani, from Masruq ibn al-Ajda', from Ibn Mas'ud: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"5082","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Kaysan, from Abdillah ibn Shaddad, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The closest of you to me on the Day of Resurrection are those who send the most blessings upon me."
"5083","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ziyad ibn al-Jarrah, from Ibn Ma'qil who said: I entered with my father upon Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, and I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remorse is repentance."
"5084","Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Ibn Mas'ud who said: We used to say when we sat in prayer: Peace be upon Allah before His servants, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mika'il, peace be upon so-and-so. He said: Then we would say: His angels. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to us and said: Allah is Peace; when you sit, say: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but He, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then choose speech."
"5085","Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman should not touch another woman and then describe her to her husband, as if he is looking at her."
"5086","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Rifa'ah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Black banners will come from the east, and horses will wade through blood up to their fetlocks; they will proclaim justice and seek justice but will not be given it, then they will prevail, then justice will be sought from them but they will not give it."
"5087","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Uqbah al-Shaybani narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the mosque, and there were women of the Ansar in it, so he came to them, exhorted them and reminded them, and said: There is no woman among you whose three children die but she will enter Paradise. A woman of the noblest of them said: O Messenger of Allah, what about one with two? He said: There is no woman among you whose two die but she will enter Paradise."
"5088","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, Abu Hanifah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best Hajj is ajj and thajj. As for ajj, it is talbiyah; and as for thajj, it is slaughtering camels."
"5089","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi, from Abu Ubaydah, from his father Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is jealous for His believing servant, so let him be jealous for himself."
"5090","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not a slanderer, nor a curser, nor obscene, nor foul-mouthed."
"5091","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Suddi who said: I asked Murrah al-Hamdani about His saying: There is none of you but will come to it, and he narrated to me that Abdullah narrated to them, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: They will come to the Bridge and leave it according to their deeds; the first of them will pass like the wind, then like the gallop of a horse, then like a rider on his mount, then like a man's running, then like his walking."
"5092","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies setting up an equal to Allah will enter the Fire. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And another I said: Whoever dies not setting up an equal to Allah, Allah will admit him to Paradise. And these obligatory prayers are expiations for the sins between them, as long as murder is avoided. Abu Bakr said: Meaning: major sins."
"5093","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah who said: A man was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so slept the night until morning. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan urinated in his ear."
"5094","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Isa ibn Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Taking omens is shirk; there is none of us but, but Allah removes it by trust in Him."
"5095","Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yazid ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is as if I am looking at Musa son of Imran in this valley, entering ihram between two striped garments."
"5096","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Those before you of the Children of Israel, when a doer among them did a sin, the forbidding one forbade him by way of excuse, but the next day he would sit with him, eat with him and drink with him, as if he had not seen him upon sin yesterday. When Allah saw that of them, He struck the hearts of some of them upon others, and cursed them upon the tongue of their Prophet Dawud and Isa son of Maryam: That was because they disobeyed and transgressed. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, you must command good, and you must forbid evil, and you must bend him to the truth completely, or Allah will strike the hearts of some of you upon others, and curse you as He cursed them."
"5097","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdillah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that some people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Our companion is ill; shall we cauterize him? He said: So he fell silent for a while, then said: If you wish, cauterize him, and if you wish, sprinkle hot stones on him."
"5098","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Sallam ibn Sulayman Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Zirr, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: I was among sheep belonging to the family of Abu Mu'ayt, herding them, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me with Abu Bakr ibn Abi Quhafah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O boy, do you have milk to give us to drink? I said: Yes, but I am entrusted. He said: Do you have a young ewe upon which no male has mounted? I said: Yes, and I brought him a young ewe. Sallam said: Upon which no male has mounted, and it is one that has no udder. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped the place of the udder though it had no udder, and there was a full udder filled with milk. I brought him a hollowed rock, and he milked, gave Abu Bakr to drink, gave me to drink, then drank, then said to the udder: Shrink. So it returned as it was. He said: I saw this with my own eyes from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me. He wiped my head and said: May Allah bless you, for you are a taught boy. So I became Muslim, and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). While we were with him on Hira, Surat al-Mursalat was revealed to him, and I learned it while his mouth was still moist with it; I do not know with which of the two verses it was sealed: And when it is said to them, bow, they do not bow, or: In what speech after it will they believe. I took seventy surahs from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and took the rest of the Qur'an from his companions. He said: While we were sleeping on Hira, nothing woke us but the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The one who kept it from you kept you from it. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is that? He said: A snake that came out from the side of the mountain."
"5099","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that Musaylimah sent two men, one of them Ibn Uthal ibn Hujr, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? They said: We bear witness that Musaylimah is the Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in Allah and His messengers; had I been one to kill envoys, I would have killed you both. While Ibn Mas'ud was in Kufah, the man who was with Ibn Uthal, a relative of his, was brought to him, so he ordered his killing. He said to the people: Do you know why I killed him? They said: We do not know. He said: Musaylimah sent him with Ibn Uthal ibn Hujr, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? They said: We bear witness that Musaylimah is the Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in Allah and His messengers; had I been one to kill envoys, I would have killed you both. He said: So for that I killed him. Abu Wa'il said: And the man was then a disbeliever."
"5100","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which sin is greatest with Allah? He said: That you set up an equal to Allah though He created you. He said: Then which? He said: Then that you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife. He said: So Allah revealed its confirmation: And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul Allah forbade except in truth, nor commit adultery."
"5101","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to be judged on the Day of Resurrection among people will be concerning blood."
"5102","And from al-A'mash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd: Abdullah narrated to us two hadiths: one from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the other from himself. He said: The believer sees his sins as if sitting beneath a mountain, fearing it will fall upon him, while the wicked sees his sins like a fly that passed over his nose, and he said to it like this. He said: And he said: Allah is more joyful at the repentance of the servant than a man who alighted in a destructive wilderness with his mount bearing his food and drink; he laid his head down and slept a sleep, then woke to find his mount gone with his food and drink upon it. He set out seeking it until thirst or hunger overcame him - Abu Shihab doubted - He said: I will return to my place and die in it. So he returned to his place, laid his head down, then woke to find his mount beside him, with his food and drink upon it."
"5103","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid Abu al-Fadl narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say takbir in every rising and lowering, standing and sitting, and so did Abu Bakr and Umar."
"5104","And from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheeks was seen."
"5105","Al-Abbas narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from Ubaydah al-Salmani, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of my nation are the generation who follow me, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then there will come a people whose testimony will precede their oath, and their oath their testimony. He said: So Ibrahim said: We were forbidden to swear by covenants and testimonies."
"5106","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ghuniyyah narrated to us, from his father, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed some poetry is wisdom."
"5107","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah who said: There was a man of great wealth; when death came to him, he said to his family: If you do what I command you, I will bequeath you much wealth. They said: Yes. He said: When I die, burn me, then grind me, and when it is a windy day, climb to the top of a mountain and scatter me, for if Allah decrees upon me, He will not forgive me. So that was done to him, and he was gathered in the Hand of Allah, Who said: What carried you to do what you did? He said: O Lord, fear of You. He said: Then go, for I have forgiven you."
"5108","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: So-and-so slept last night missing prayer. He said: Satan urinated in his ear - or his ears."
"5109","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers."
"5110","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl, that Abu Musa and Salman ibn Rabi'ah were asked about a daughter, a son's daughter, and a sister, and they said: To the sister is half, and to the daughter is half. Then Abdullah was asked, and he said: I would have strayed then, and I would not be of the guided; I say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To the daughter is half, to the son's daughter is a sixth completing two-thirds, and what remains is to the sister."
"5111","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Fitr ibn Khalifah, from Ata who said: Abu al-Darda said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left us, and there was no bird flying in the sky with its wings but he reminded us some knowledge of it."
"5112","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah who said: We came with Abdullah to Uthman, and Uthman said to Abdullah: What remains of you for women? He said: Come, O Alqamah - and I was a youth - So I came near, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to young bachelors and said: Whoever of you has means, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards the private part; and whoever does not, fasting is a restraint for him."
"5113","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Let those of understanding and intellect stand nearest to me, then those who follow them; and do not differ, lest your hearts differ; and beware the commotions of the markets."
"5114","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Dharr, from Wa'il ibn Mahanah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity, O assembly of women, for you are the most numerous of the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection. A woman who was not of the eminent women said: Why are we the most numerous of the people of Hell? He said: You curse much and deny the husband. Ibn Mas'ud said: I have not found any deficient in intellect and religion more overpowering over resolute men in their affairs than these women. It was said: O Ibn Mas'ud, what is the deficiency of their intellects and religion? He said: As for the deficiency of their intellects: the testimony of two women equals the testimony of one man; and as for the deficiency of their religion: there comes upon one of them whatever Allah wills of days and nights in which she does not prostrate a single prostration to Allah."
"5115","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur and Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Will we be taken for what we did in ignorance? He said: If you do good in Islam, you will not be taken for it, but if you do evil in Islam, you will be taken for the first and the last."
"5116","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A woman should not touch another woman, describing her to her husband or describing her to a man, as if he is looking at her; and if there are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of their companion, for that grieves him; and whoever swears a false oath to cut off thereby the property of his brother or the property of a Muslim man will meet Allah while He is angry with him. He said: Al-Ash'ath ibn Qays heard Ibn Mas'ud mention this hadith, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it concerning two men disputing over a well."
"5117","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Ibn Mas'ud who said: A man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), of the people of al-Suffah, died and left two dinars, and that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Two brands."
"5118","Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zayd al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Abu Muhammad, freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Abu Ubaydah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sends forth three who have not reached puberty, they will be for him a fortified fortress from the Fire. Abu Dharr said: I sent forth two, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And two. Ubayy ibn Ka'b, Abu al-Mundhir, master of reciters, said: I sent forth one, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: And one. He said: But that is at the first shock."
"5119","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Hajari, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays well where people see him, and prays badly in private, that is contempt with which he has held his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, in contempt."
"5120","Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Hajari, from Abu al-Ahwas - Abu Ya'la said: I think it is from Ibn Mas'ud - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The poor person is not the one who goes around you whom a morsel or two morsels, and a date or two dates, turn away. We said: Then who is the poor person, O Messenger of Allah? He said: One who does not find what suffices him, is shy to ask people, and is not noticed so that charity is given to him."
"5121","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Hajari, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Reviling a Muslim, his brother, is wickedness, fighting him is disbelief, and the sanctity of his wealth is like the sanctity of his blood."
"5122","And with his chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When your servant brings your food to you, let him begin and feed him a morsel, or let him sit with him, for he has endured its heat and smoke."
"5123","And from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do you know which charity is best? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: A gift: that you grant your brother dinars, or dirhams, or a cow, or a sheep, or the back of a mount, or the milk of a ewe, or the milk of a cow; and he did not say: the cow and the sheep."
"5124","And from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Satan has despaired that idols be worshipped in the land of the Arabs, but he will be content with less than that from you: with belittled sins, and they are the destroyers on the Day of Resurrection. Fear injustices as much as you can, for the servant will come with good deeds on the Day of Resurrection, thinking they will save him, and a servant will keep standing, saying: O Lord, Your servant wronged me. So He will say: Erase from his good deeds. It will remain so until no good deed of his sins remains. The like of that is like travelers who alighted in a barren land with no firewood with them; the people scattered to gather wood, and soon gathered wood, kindled a great fire, and cooked what they wished; and so are sins."
"5125","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Hajari, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah who said: None is more jealous than Allah, and out of His jealousy He forbade indecencies, what is apparent of them and what is hidden."
"5126","And from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah will command a caller on the Day of Resurrection: O Adam, stand and send forth from your offspring a delegation to the Fire. So Adam will stand and say: O Lord, out of every how many? He will say: Out of every hundred, ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise. That weighed heavily upon those Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who heard it, and they said to him: Who among us will be saved after this? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are among two creations of people: Ya'juj and Ma'juj, and they come forth from every elevation; and you in this world are only like a mark on the foreleg of a beast, or like a hair on the flank of a camel."
"5127","And from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Hands are three: the Hand of Allah Almighty is the highest, the hand of the giver which follows it, and the hand of the beggar is the lowest until the Day of Resurrection. So refrain from asking and begging as much as you can; if you are given something - or he said: good - let it be seen upon you, begin with those you support, give from surplus, and you are not blamed for refraining."
"5128","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Simak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: May Allah brighten a man who hears a hadith from us and memorizes it until he conveys it."
"5129","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he went to relieve himself, and said: Seek three stones for me. I found only two stones and dung, so he took the two stones and threw away the dung, and said: This is filth."
"5130","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yahya and Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, and Alqamah, from Abdullah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say takbir in every lowering and rising, standing and sitting, and would give salam to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheek was seen; and Abu Bakr and Umar used to do that."
"5131","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Abd al-Karim al-Jazari narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam, from Abdillah ibn Ma'qil who said: I entered with my father upon Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, and he said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Remorse is repentance? He said: Yes."
"5132","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which sin is greatest with Allah? He said: That you set up an equal to Allah though He created you. He said: I said: That is indeed great. He said: I said: Then which? He said: That you kill your child fearing he will eat with you. He said: I said: Then which? He said: That you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife."
"5133","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah who said: Some people said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Will we be taken for what we did in ignorance? He said: As for whoever of you does good in Islam, he will not be taken for it; and whoever does evil will be taken for his deeds in ignorance and Islam."
"5134","And with his chain, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are three, two men should not converse privately to the exclusion of the other until you mix with people, because that grieves him; and a woman should not touch another woman and describe her to her husband, as if he is looking at her."
"5135","And from Abdullah who said: On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) favored in the spoils, giving al-Aqra' ibn Habis one hundred camels, giving Uyaynah the like, giving some nobles of the Arabs, favoring them in the division. A man said: By Allah, this is a division in which justice was not done, and the Face of Allah was not intended by it. He said: So I said: By Allah, I will inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I came to him and informed him of what the man said. He said: His face changed until it was like saffron dye. Then he said: Then who is just, if the Messenger of Allah is not just? Then he said: May Allah have mercy on Musa; he was harmed with more than this, yet he was patient. So I said: Of course, I will not raise anything to him after this."
"5136","From Abu Wail, he said: Abdullah said: A man came to me today and asked me about a matter I did not know how to answer him. He said: What do you think of an active and energetic man who goes out on military expeditions, and they impose upon us matters from which we find no escape? He said: So I said to him: By Allah, I do not know what to say to you, except that we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it would be that he would not impose upon us a matter except once until we did it. And indeed one of you will remain upon good as long as he fears Allah, and when he doubts something within himself he asks a man and he cures him, and it is imminent that you will not find him. By Him besides whom there is no god, I do not recall what has passed of this world except as like a pond whose clear water has been drunk and whose murky water remains."
"5137","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir meaning Ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: We used to say in prayer behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Peace be upon so-and-so. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us one day: Indeed Allah is al-Salam, so when one of you sits in prayer let him say: All greetings, prayers and good words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah - for when he says it, it reaches every righteous servant in heaven and earth - I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then let him choose whatever supplication he wishes."
"5138","And with his chain of narration, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: How bad it is for one of you to say: I forgot such-and-such verse, rather he was made to forget. Remind yourselves of the Quran, for it escapes from the breasts of men more intensely than camels escape from their hobbles."
"5139","And from Abu Wail, he said: Abdullah used to remind the people every Thursday, so a man said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, if only you would remind us every day? He said: As for that, what prevents me from that is that I dislike to bore you, and I visit you with admonition just as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit us with admonition in those days, fearing weariness upon us."
"5140","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Truthfulness guides to righteousness, and righteousness guides to Paradise, and a man keeps telling the truth until he is recorded as a truthful one. And lying guides to wickedness, and wickedness guides to the Fire, and a man keeps lying until he is recorded with Allah as a liar."
"5141","And from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I know the last of the people of the Fire to come out of it, and the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise: a man who will come out of the Fire crawling, so Allah will say: Go and enter Paradise. So he will come to it and it will appear to him as if it is full, so Allah will say: Enter, for you shall have the like of the world and ten times its like. He said: So he will say: Are You mocking me - or laughing at me - while You are the King? He said: Then I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laugh until his molars appeared. He said: And it used to be said: That is the lowest of the people of Paradise in rank."
"5142","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abidah al-Salmani, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which people are best? He said: My generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose testimony will precede their oath and whose oath will precede their testimony. Ibrahim said: They used to forbid us, when we were children, from oaths and testimonies."
"5143","And from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah said: May Allah curse the tattooing women and the women who are tattooed, the women who pluck eyebrows and those who have it done, and the women who separate their teeth for beauty, who change the creation of Allah. He said: That reached a woman from Banu Asad called Umm Yaqub who used to recite the Quran, so she came and said: What is this hadith that reached me from you, that you cursed the tattooing women and the women who are tattooed, the women who pluck eyebrows and the women who separate teeth for beauty, who change the creation of Allah? So Abdullah said: Why should I not curse those whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed, while it is in the Book of Allah? The woman said: I have read what is between the two covers of the mushaf and I did not find it. So he said: By Allah, if you had read it you would have found it. Then he said: {And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it}. The woman said: Then I see some of this upon your wife. He said: Then go and look. He said: So she entered upon the wife of Abdullah and saw nothing. So she came to him and said: I did not see anything. He said: Had that been so, we would not have kept her company."
"5144","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer - Ibrahim said: I do not know whether he added or decreased - so when he gave salam, it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, has something new happened in the prayer? He said: No, and what is that? They said: You prayed such-and-such. He said: So he folded his leg, faced the qiblah, prostrated two prostrations, then gave salam. Then when he gave salam he turned to us with his face and said: Had something new happened in the prayer I would have informed you of it, but I am only a human like you, I forget as you forget, so when I forget remind me, and when one of you doubts in his prayer let him seek what is correct and complete upon it, then give salam, then prostrate two prostrations."
"5145","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from his father, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none among you except that a companion from the jinn has been assigned to him. They said: And you too, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And me too, except that Allah helped me against him so he submitted, and he commands me with nothing but good."
"5146","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Dharr, from Wail ibn Muhanah of Taym, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O assembly of women, give charity even from your jewelry, for you are the majority of the people of Hell. So a woman who was not among the prominent women said: Why are we, O Messenger of Allah, the majority of the people of Hell? He said: Because you excessively curse and deny the kindness of the husband."
"5147","And from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when he saw the people turning away: O Allah, seven like the seven of Yusuf. So a famine seized them that consumed everything, until they ate dead meat, skins and carcasses, and one of them would look to the sky and see smoke from hunger. So Abu Sufyan came to him and said: O Muhammad, you came commanding obedience to Allah and joining of kinship, yet your people have perished, so supplicate to Allah for them. Allah said: {So watch for the day when the sky will bring a clear smoke} up to His saying: {Indeed We will take retribution}."
"5148","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, he said: Shibak mentioned to Ibrahim, he said: We asked Alqamah about that, so he narrated to us from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of riba and its giver. He said: So I said: And its two witnesses and its scribe? He said: We only narrate what we heard."
"5149","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: Hunayy al-Dabbi said: We met Alqamah - while Ziyad had mutilated a man he crucified - so he said to us: For what have these gathered? I said: Ziyad mutilated a man. He said: Abdullah said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as I recall: Indeed the most chaste of people in killing are the people of faith."
"5150","And from Mughirah, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The child belongs to the owner of the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"5151","And from Mughirah, from Wasil ibn Hayyan, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Had I been taking a close friend from the people of the earth, I would have taken Abu Bakr ibn Abi Quhafah as a close friend, but your Companion is the close friend of Allah. And the Quran was revealed upon seven letters, for every verse thereof is an outer and an inner meaning, and for every limit is an ascent."
"5152","And from Jarir, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu Hayyan, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite to me. I said: Did I not learn from you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I love to hear it from other than me. So I recited to him Surat al-Nisa until when I reached: {So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness, and We bring you as a witness over these?} his eyes overflowed."
"5153","And from Jarir, he said: And al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi ibn Umaylah al-Fazari narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Hassan, from his uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Abdullah, he said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked ten characteristics: wearing a gold ring, trailing the lower garment, yellow dye - meaning khaluq perfume - changing grey hair - Jarir said: meaning plucking it - ruqyah except with the two Muawwidhat, tying amulets, striking with dice, displaying adornment to other than its proper place, withholding water from its proper place, and corrupting the child without prohibiting him."
"5154","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abu Sad al-Azdi, from Abu al-Kanud, he said: I captured a man from the nobles of Persia on the day of Mihran. He said: So I raised his spoil to the ruler. He said: So I took a gold ring of his. He said: And it had been seen in my hand. He said: I said: When I go out to the land of the non-Arabs and something befalls me, it will be marketable. So I entered upon Abdullah while it was in my hand, so he said: What is this ring? So I related the story to him, so he took it from me, placed it in his mouth then chewed it, then threw it to me, then said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the gold ring."
"5155","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, he said: I heard Abdullah saying: Your Prophet was given of everything except the keys of the five: {Indeed with Allah is the knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs} the whole verse."
"5156","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yahya al-Jabir, from Abu Majidah, from Abdullah, he said: We asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about walking with the funeral, so he said: Walking is slower than trotting; if it be good it is hastened to it, and if it be other than that, then away with the people of the Fire. The funeral is to be followed, and he who goes ahead of it is not of it."
"5157","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yahya al-Jabir, from Abu Majidah, from Abdullah, that he began narrating, he said: Indeed the first man whose hand was cut among the Muslims - or among the Muslims - was a man from the Ansar; he was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was said: He stole. So he said: Take your companion and cut him. It was as if the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sprinkled with ashes. So one of his companions said to him: As if this has grieved you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And how should you not be supporters of Satan - or of Iblis? Indeed it is not fitting for one in charge of an affair that a prescribed punishment be brought to him except that he carries it out. And Allah is Pardoning and loves pardon. Then he recited this verse: {And let them pardon and overlook. Do you not love that Allah should forgive you?}"
"5158","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki and Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed there will be after me favoritism and matters you will disapprove of. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command whoever among us reaches that? He said: You will render the right that is upon you, and ask Allah for that which is yours."
"5159","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he is the truthful one believed - said: Indeed the creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's belly for forty days, then he becomes a clot like that, then he becomes a lump like that, then Allah sends the angel with four words: his provision, his deed, his term, and whether wretched or happy. By Him in whose Hand is my soul, one of you does the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is nothing between him and it except a cubit, then what was written for him in the Book overtakes him and he does the deeds of the people of the Fire and enters it. And one of you does the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is nothing between him and it except a cubit, then what was written for him in the Book overtakes him and he does the deeds of the people of Paradise and enters it."
"5160","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave, there was revealed to him: {By those sent forth in succession} - so we learned it from his mouth while his mouth was still moist with it - when a snake came out. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill it. He said: So we rushed toward it and it outran us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was protected from your evil and you were protected from its evil."
"5161","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: When this verse was revealed: {Those who believed and did not mix their faith with wrongdoing} it weighed heavily upon the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they said: Which of us has not mixed his faith with wrongdoing? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not that; have you not heard the saying of Luqman: {Indeed associating partners with Allah is a tremendous wrong}?"
"5162","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: A man from the People of the Book came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Indeed Allah holds the heavens upon a finger, the earths upon a finger, the mountains and trees upon a finger, the water and soil upon a finger, and all creatures upon a finger, then He says: I am the King. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars appeared, then he recited this verse: {And they did not esteem Allah as He deserves to be esteemed, while the earth entirely will be His grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens folded in His right hand} the verse. So I said to Ibrahim: In this world or in the Hereafter? So he said: In this world."
"5163","And from Abdullah, he said: I was on Friday night in the mosque when a man from the Ansar entered and said: If a man found another man with his wife, if he speaks you will flog him, if he kills you will kill him, and if he keeps silent he keeps silent in anger. By Allah, I shall surely ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it. So when it was the next day, he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, saying: If a man found another man with his wife and he speaks you will flog him, or he kills you will kill him, or he keeps silent he keeps silent in anger. He said: O Allah, open. And he began supplicating. Then the verse of mutual cursing was revealed: {And those who accuse their wives and have no witnesses but themselves} these verses. So the man was tried with it among the people. So he and his wife came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they invoked curses upon each other. So the man bore witness four testimonies by Allah that he was among the truthful, then he invoked the curse the fifth time: that the curse of Allah be upon him if he were among the liars. Then she went to invoke the curse, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wait. So she invoked it. Then when they turned away, he said: Perhaps she will bring him black and curly-haired. So she brought him black and curly-haired."
"5164","And from Ibrahim, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whom do you count as childless among you? He said: We said: The one who has no child. He said: That is not the childless one; rather the childless one is he who has not sent forth anything of his children. He said: And whom do you count as the strong wrestler among you? He said: We said: The one whom men cannot throw down. He said: That is not so; rather it is he who controls himself at anger."
"5165","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, he said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of you is his wealth dearer to him than the wealth of his heir? They said: O Messenger of Allah, there is none among us except that his wealth is dearer to him than the wealth of his heir. He said: Know what you say. They said: We know nothing but that, O Messenger of Allah. He said: There is no man among you except that the wealth of his heir is dearer to him than his wealth? They said: How, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Indeed the wealth of one of you is only what he has sent forth, and the wealth of his heir is what he has left behind."
"5166","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, he said: Abdullah said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was feverish, so I touched him with my hand and said: O Messenger of Allah, you are indeed suffering a severe fever. The Messenger of Allah said: Yes, I am afflicted as two men among you are afflicted. So I said: Is that because you have two rewards? So the Messenger of Allah said: Yes. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim is afflicted with harm from illness or anything besides it, except that Allah removes thereby some of his sins, just as the tree sheds its leaves."
"5167","And from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he lengthened it until I intended an evil matter. He said: And what did you intend? He said: I intended to sit down and leave him."
"5168","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about a man who loves a people but has not joined them? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is with those he loves."
"5169","And from Abu Wail, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, which sin is greatest with Allah? He said: That you call upon a rival for Allah while He created you. He said: Then which? He said: Then that you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife. He said: So Allah revealed confirming it: {And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right} the verse."
"5170","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, he said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your predecessor at the Pool; men among you will be contested with me over it, then I shall surely be overcome regarding them, and it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"5171","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one to whom praise is dearer than Allah, Mighty and Majestic; for that reason He praised Himself. And there is no one more jealous than Allah; for that reason He forbade immoralities."
"5172","And from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not a woman touch another woman so as to describe her to her husband, as if he were looking at her."
"5173","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: A man asked me today about something I did not know what to say to him. He said: What do you think of an active, energetic man keen on jihad, while our commanders impose upon us matters we cannot enumerate? He said: So I said: By Allah, I do not know what to say to you, except that we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it would be that he would not command us with anything except that we did it. And what remains of this world resembles nothing but a pond whose clear water has been drunk and whose murky water remains. And indeed one of you will remain upon good as long as he fears Allah, and when something pricks his soul he comes to a man and asks him and he cures him. And by Allah, it is imminent that you will not find him."
"5174","And from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walking, and we passed by children among whom was Ibn Sayyad. So the children fled and Ibn Sayyad sat down, and it was as if the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: May your hands be dusted, do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: No, rather you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah. Umar said: Do you permit me, O Messenger of Allah, to kill him? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he is the one you see, you will not be able to kill him."
"5175","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Razin, from Zir, he said: Ibn Masud said: There was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {By those sent forth in succession} while we were in a cave, so he had me recite it, and I recite it close to how he had me recite it. And I do not know with which ending he ended: {And when it is said to them: Bow, they do not bow} or {Then in what statement after it will they believe}?"
"5176","And from al-Amash, from Umarah, from al-Aswad, he said: Abdullah said: Let none of you assign a share of himself to Satan, that he sees it as a duty upon him to leave to his right. I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaving mostly to his left. Umarah said: So I came to Madinah and saw the dwellings of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to his left."
"5177","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: Al-Ashath ibn Qays entered upon Abdullah while he was eating lunch, so he said: Come near. So al-Ashath said: Is today not the day of Ashura? So Abdullah said: And what makes you know what Ashura is? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast it, then when Ramadan was revealed he left it."
"5178","And from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: Abdullah said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray a prayer except at its time, except two prayers: I saw him pray Maghrib and Isha together at Muzdalifah, and pray the Fajr prayer before its time in darkness."
"5179","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah, meaning from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, he said: I entered upon Abdullah visiting him while he was ill, so he narrated to us two hadiths: a hadith from himself, and a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The believer sees his sins as if he were at the foot of a mountain fearing it will fall upon him, while the wicked one sees his sins like a fly that passed over his nose and he waved it away from him. He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His believing servant than a man in a desolate, deadly land, with him his mount bearing his food and drink. So he slept, then woke to find it gone. So he stood seeking it, and sought it until thirst overtook him. Then he said: I shall return to the place where I was until I die. He said: So he placed his head upon his forearm to die. Then he woke to find his mount beside him bearing his provision, food and drink. So Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than this one at his mount and provision."
"5180","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one to whom praise is dearer than Allah; for that reason He praised Himself. And there is no one more jealous than Allah; for that reason He forbade immoralities. And there is no one to whom excuse is dearer than Allah; for that reason He sent down the Book and sent the Messengers."
"5181","And from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah al-Hamdani, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no soul killed unjustly except that upon the first son of Adam is a share of its blood, because he initiated killing."
"5182","And from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am quit of every close friend's friendship, and had I been taking a close friend I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, and indeed your Companion is the close friend of Allah."
"5183","And from Jarir, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Awsajah ibn al-Rammah, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, You have made my creation good, so make my character good."
"5184","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Umarah ibn al-Qaqa, from Abu Zurah, he said: A companion of ours narrated to us, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing transmits disease to anything - three times. So a Bedouin among the people said: O Messenger of Allah, a camel may be among great camels and it has a sore on its tail or its lip, then all the camels become mangy. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then who made the first one mangy? Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion, no evil omen, no Safar, and no Hamah. Allah created every soul and wrote its life, its provision, and its afflictions."
"5185","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Wail, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: Indeed Allah has not sent down a disease except that He has made for it a cure; whoever knows it knows it, and whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it."
"5186","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to relieve himself, so he relieved himself, then said: Bring me something with which to clean myself, and do not bring me a bone nor dung. He said: Then he performed ablution and stood praying, and I saw him whenever he bowed he bent down - meaning he joined his hands and placed them between his knees. Layth said: Al-hail means the bone."
"5187","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, he said: I was with Abdullah until he reached the Jamrat al-Aqabah and I went ahead of him. So he said: Hand me stones. So I handed him seven stones while he was reciting talbiyah. Then he said: Take the halter of the she-camel. So he came to the bottom of the valley, turned toward the tree, then said: Allah is Greatest, then threw, making takbir with every pebble until he threw seven pebbles. Then he said: O Allah, make it an accepted hajj and a forgiven sin. Then he said: Thus did the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed."
"5188","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it upon its destruction in truth, and another to whom Allah has given wisdom, so he judges by it and teaches it."
"5189","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, he said: Abdullah said: On the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you think about these captives? Abdullah ibn Rawahah said: O Messenger of Allah, you are in a valley full of firewood, so kindle the valley with fire upon them, then cast them into it. Al-Abbas said: May Allah cut your kinship. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, the leaders and chiefs of the polytheists, they belied you and fought you, strike their necks. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, your kin and your people, spare them; Allah may rescue them through you from the Fire. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered to relieve himself. A group said: The word is what Umar said, and a group said: The word is what Abu Bakr said. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said: What is your opinion about these two men? Their example is like brothers of theirs who were before them. Nuh said: {My Lord, leave not upon the earth any dweller from the disbelievers. Indeed if You leave them they will mislead Your servants}. And Musa said: {Our Lord, obliterate their wealth and harden their hearts so they will not believe until they see the painful punishment}. And Ibrahim (peace be upon him) said: {So whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me, then indeed You are Forgiving, Merciful}. And Isa said: {If You punish them, they are Your servants, and if You forgive them, indeed You are the Mighty, the Wise}. And you are a people with dependents, so let none of you return except with a ransom or a striking of the neck. Abdullah said: I said: Except Sahl ibn Bayda, let him not be killed, for I heard him speaking Islam. So he fell silent. No day came upon me more fearful to me, lest stones be cast upon me from the sky, than that day of mine, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Except Sahl ibn Bayda."
"5190","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: We used to greet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in prayer and he would return it to us. Then when we returned from the Negus we greeted him and he did not return it to us. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to greet you in prayer and you would return it to us. So he said: Indeed in prayer there is occupation."
"5191","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Mutarrif ibn Tarif narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahm, from Abu al-Radrad, from Abdullah, he said: We used to greet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer and he would return it to us. Then one day I greeted him and he did not return it to me, so I felt something within myself. Then when he finished I said: O Messenger of Allah, when I used to greet you in prayer you would return it to me? He said: So he said: Indeed Allah introduces from His command whatever He wills."
"5192","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed the excellence of a man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-some degrees."
"5193","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Harun ibn Antarah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, he said: Alqamah and al-Aswad sought permission from Abdullah after they had sat long at his door until midday. He said: So I went out and sought permission for them, and he permitted them. So he said to them: Why did you not enter? He said: They said: We thought you were sleeping. He said: I would not like you to think this of me. We used to equate the prayer of this hour with the night prayer, or nearly the night prayer. Then he said: Rulers will come over you who will be distracted from the time of prayer, so pray it at its time. Then he stood and prayed between him and them, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5194","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: I was walking with Abdullah at Mina when he met Uthman, so he stood with him conversing. So Uthman said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, shall we not marry you to a young maiden who may remind you of what has passed of your time? Abdullah said: If you say that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: O assembly of youth, whoever among you can afford marriage let him marry, for it is more lowering for the gaze and more guarding for the private parts, and whoever cannot, upon him is fasting, for it is a shield for him."
"5195","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah recited Surat Yusuf at Hims, so a man said: It was not revealed like this. So Abdullah drew near him and smelled wine upon him. So he said: Do you belie the truth and drink filth? By Allah, thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) have me recite it. By Allah, I shall not leave you until I flog you the prescribed punishment. He said: So he flogged him the punishment."
"5196","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he said: Uthman prayed four at Mina. He said: So Abdullah said to him: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina two rakahs, and with Abu Bakr two rakahs, and with Umar two rakahs. Then the paths diverged with you, and I would love that for me, out of four rakahs, two accepted rakahs."
"5197","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: Abdullah stoned the Jamrat al-Aqabah from the bottom of the valley with seven pebbles, making takbir with every pebble. He said: So it was said to him: People stone it from above it. So Abdullah said: This, by Him besides whom there is no god, is the station of the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed."
"5198","And from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abu Mamar, from Abdullah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina when the moon split, until a part of it went behind the mountain. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bear witness."
"5199","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath while sinful therein, to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim man, will meet Allah while He is angry with him. Al-Ashath said: By Allah, it was about me; there was between me and a Jewish man a land and he denied me it, so I brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah said to me: Do you have proof? He said: I said: No. He said to the Jew: Swear. He said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, then he will swear and take my wealth. So Allah revealed: {Indeed those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price}."
"5200","Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one word, and I said another. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise. He said: And I said: And whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire."
"5201","And with his chain, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your predecessor at the Pool, and peoples will be contested with me over it, then I shall surely be overcome regarding them. So I shall say: O Lord, my companions. Then He will say: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"5202","And from al-Amash, from Shimr, from Mughirah ibn Sad ibn al-Akhram, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take estates lest you desire the world. Then Abdullah said: And in Madinah what is in Madinah, and in Radhan what is in Radhan."
"5203","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who strikes cheeks, tears pockets, and calls with the call of the people of Jahiliyyah."
"5204","And from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood of a Muslim man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except by one of three: the married adulterer, a soul for a soul, and the one who abandons his religion and separates from the community."
"5205","And from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: When one of you bows let him spread his forearms upon his thighs and crouch. He said: It is as if I am looking at the dispersion of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Then he joined his palms and showed them."
"5206","Al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he said: I was concealed by the curtains of the Kabah. He said: So three men came, abundant in the fat of their bellies, scant in the understanding of their hearts. He said: A Qurashi and his two Thaqafi in-laws, or a Thaqafi and his two Qurashi in-laws. So they spoke words I did not understand. So one of them said: Do you think Allah hears this speech of ours? The other said: When we raise our voices He hears it, and when we do not raise it He does not hear it. The other said: If He hears anything of it, He hears all of it. He said: So I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so there was revealed to him: {And you were not concealed lest your hearing, your sights and your skins testify against you} up to His saying: {So you became among the losers}."
"5207","And from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrating a prophet whom his people struck, while he wipes the blood from his face and says: My Lord, forgive my people, for they do not know."
"5208","And from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed a distribution, so a man from the Ansar said: This is a distribution by which the Face of Allah was not intended. He said: So Abdullah said: So I said: O enemy of Allah, I shall surely inform the Messenger of Allah of what you said. He said: So I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So his face reddened, and he said: May Allah have mercy upon Musa; he was harmed with more than this and he was patient."
"5209","And al-Amash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: That I swear by Allah nine times that Ibn Said is the Dajjal is dearer to me than that I swear once, and that I swear nine times that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was killed by killing is dearer to me than that I swear once. And that is because Allah took him as a prophet and made him a martyr."
"5210","And al-Amash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from the nephew of Zaynab, from Zaynab the wife of Abdullah, from Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed ruqyah, amulets and tiwalah are shirk. She said: So I said: Why do you say this? My eye used to discharge, and I used to go to so-and-so the Jew who would charm it; when he charmed it, it would settle. He said: That is only the work of Satan; he used to prick it with his hand, and when you charmed it he would desist from it. It would have sufficed you to say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, and You are the Healer, a healing that leaves no sickness."
"5211","And al-Amash narrated to us, from Muslim, from Masruq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers."
"5212","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Khishf ibn Malik, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the blood-money in accidental killing in fifths."
"5213","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is nearer to one of you than the strap of his sandal, and the Fire is likewise."
"5214","And from al-Amash, from al-Dahhak, he said: I was with Masruq in a portico in which there were statues, so he looked at one of them, and they said: This is a statue of Maryam. So Masruq said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers."
"5215","And from Waki, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib, from Zad han, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah has angels roaming the earth conveying to me greetings from my ummah."
"5216","Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."
"5217","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing judged among people on the Day of Resurrection will be regarding blood."
"5218","And from Abdullah, he said: It is as if I am looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrating a prophet among the prophets whom his people struck, while he wipes the blood from his face and says: My Lord, forgive my people, for they do not know."
"5219","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begs while having wealth that suffices him will come on the Day of Resurrection with scratches, gashes upon his face. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is his sufficiency? He said: Fifty dirhams or its equivalent in gold."
"5220","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in al-Najm, and the Muslims prostrated, except a man from Quraysh who took a handful of dust, raised it to his forehead and prostrated upon it. Abdullah said: So I saw him killed as a disbeliever."
"5221","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Isa ibn Asim al-Asadi, from Zir, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Evil omen is shirk, and there is none among us except... but Allah removes it through reliance."
"5222","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are three, let not two converse privately to the exclusion of one, for that grieves him."
"5223","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, he said: Abdullah said to Ibn al-Nawwahah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Were it not that you are a messenger I would have killed you. As for today, you are no messenger. Stand, O Kharashah, and strike his neck."
"5224","Al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, he said: A man came to Abdullah and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, how do you recite this verse: {From water unaltered}? He said: So Abdullah said to him: Have you mastered all the Quran except this? He said: I recite the Mufassal in one rakah. So Abdullah said to him: Like the hasty recitation of poetry? Indeed among the best of prayer are bowing and prostration. And peoples will recite the Quran and it will not pass their collarbones, but when it is recited and takes root in the heart it benefits. I know the pairs which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in every rakah. Then he stood, and Alqamah entered upon him. Then he said: Ask him for us about the pairs which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite. He said: Then he came out to us and said: Twenty surahs from the Mufassal in the arrangement of Abdullah."
"5225","And from Abdullah, he said: We were walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he passed by Ibn al-Sayyad. So the Messenger of Allah said: I have hidden for you something hidden. So Ibn al-Sayyad said: Al-dukhkh. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be despised, you will not exceed your measure."
"5226","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sleep lying on his back until he snored, then he would stand and pray without performing ablution."
"5227","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Ibrahim, he said: Alqamah led us in prayer and prayed five. So the people murmured and criticized him. He said: So I said: You have done it. He said: And you, O one-eyed one, say that? He said: So he turned and prostrated two prostrations, then narrated to them from Abdullah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed five with them, so he was told about that, so he turned and prostrated two prostrations, and said: I am only a human; I forget as you forget."
"5228","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Amash mentioning from Shaqiq, he said: Abdullah used to come out to us and say: I am informed of your place, and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except dislike of boring you. Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit us with admonition in those days, disliking weariness upon us."
"5229","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it upon its destruction in truth, and a man to whom Allah has given wisdom, so he judges by it and teaches it."
"5230","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite to me. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall I recite to you when it was only revealed to you? He said: I love to hear it from other than me. He said: So I recited to him Surat al-Nisa until I passed this verse: {So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness, and We bring you as a witness over these?} He said: So I looked at him and his eyes were shedding tears."
"5231","Waki narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: What have I to do with the world? My example and the example of the world is only like a rider who rested in the shade of a tree on a summer day, then departed and left it."
"5232","Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: When there was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {When the help of Allah comes and the victory} he would often, when he recited it and bowed, say: Glory be to You, O Allah, our Lord, and with Your praise. O Allah, forgive me. Indeed You are the Oft-Returning, the Merciful - three times."
"5233","And from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted me as extra spoil the sword of Abu Jahl on the day of Badr."
"5234","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki and Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Ubaydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the two rakahs as if upon embers. I said: Until he stands? He said: Until he stands. Waki said: Upon hot stones."
"5235","And Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, regarding the sermon of need: Indeed praise is for Allah; we seek His help and seek His forgiveness, and we seek refuge with Allah from the evils of ourselves. Whomever Allah guides none can misguide, and whomever He misguides none can guide. And I bear witness that there is no god but He, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then he recites verses from the Book of Allah: {Fear Allah as He deserves to be feared, and die not except as Muslims}, {And fear Allah through whom you ask one another, and the wombs. Indeed Allah is ever over you an Observer}, {Fear Allah and speak a right word. He will amend your deeds and forgive your sins, and whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has surely attained a tremendous success}."
"5236","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas and Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, the like of it."
"5237","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl, he said: A man came to Abu Musa and Salman ibn Rabiah and asked them about a daughter, a son's daughter, a paternal sister, and a mother. So they said: For the daughter is half, and what remains is for the sister. So the man came to Abdullah and asked him, and informed him of what they said. So he said: {I would have strayed then and would not be among the guided}. But I shall judge as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged: For the daughter is half, for the son's daughter is a sixth completing two-thirds, and what remains is for the sister."
"5238","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from Asim, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow hajj with umrah, for they remove poverty and sins just as the bellows remove the dross of iron, gold and silver. And there is no reward for an accepted hajj except Paradise."
"5239","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Shabi, from Alqamah, he said: I said to Ibn Masud: Did anyone among you accompany the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the jinn? He said: So he said: None of us accompanied him, but we missed him one night in Makkah, so we said: He was assassinated, he was snatched away. So we spent the worst night a people ever spent. Then when it was sahar - or he said: morning - we saw him coming from the direction of Hira. So we said: O Messenger of Allah. And they mentioned to him what they had been in. So he said: A caller of the jinn came to me, so I went and recited to them. Then he went and showed us their traces and the traces of their fires."
"5240","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the adhan of Bilal - or he said: the call of Bilal - prevent one of you from his sahur, for he calls adhan - or he said: calls - at night, to return your night-praying one and awaken your sleeper. And he said: It is not that you say like this and like this. And he leveled his hand and raised it until he says like this, and he separated his fingers."
"5241","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, from Ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting goods before they reach the market."
"5242","And from Ibn Masud, that a man received a kiss from a woman, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this verse was revealed: {And establish prayer at the two ends of the day}. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for me? He said: And for whoever among my ummah acts upon it."
"5243","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The eater of riba, its giver, its scribe, and its two witnesses when they know of it, the tattooing woman and the woman who is tattooed, the collector who withholds charity, and the one who reverts to Bedouin life after his migration are cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5244","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Sulayman ibn Atiq informed me, from Talq ibn Habib, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Shall I not inform you - the extremists have perished - three times."
"5245","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, my father narrated to me, from Abu Yala, from al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew for us a square line, and drew in its middle lines like this beside the line, and drew a line outside it. So he said: Do you know what this is? So we said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is man - for the line in the middle of the line - and this is his term, and these are the afflictions - for the lines - assailing him; when this one misses him that one strikes him. And that is hope - for the outer line."
"5246","Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, from al-Hakam and Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Mamar, that a governor in Makkah used to give two salams. So Abdullah said: From where did he learn it? Al-Hakam said in his hadith: Indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it."
"5247","Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Sulayman narrated to me, from Umarah, from Wahb ibn Rabiah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: I was concealed by the curtains of the Kabah when three men entered: a Thaqafi and his two Qurashi in-laws. So they conversed among themselves, and one of them said: Do you think Allah hears what we said? One of them said: He hears when we raise, and does not hear when we lower. And the other said: If He hears anything from us, He hears all of it. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so this verse was revealed: {And you were not concealed lest they testify against you} the verse."
"5248","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Mansur narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Abu Mamar, from Abdullah, similar to it."
"5249","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Were it not that you are a messenger I would have killed you - meaning the messenger of Musaylimah."
"5250","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Hour will not come except upon the worst of people."
"5251","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Shubah, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Had I been taking a close friend I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but he is my brother and my companion, and Allah has taken your Companion as a close friend."
"5252","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan does not take my likeness."
"5253","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim, from Zir, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"5254","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Zubayd, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He is not of us who strikes cheeks, tears pockets, and calls with the call of Jahiliyyah."
"5255","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Qatadah, from Usayr ibn Jabir, he said: A wind raged while we were with Abdullah, so Ibn Masud became angry until we recognized anger in his face. He said: Woe to you! The Hour will not come until no inheritance is divided and no spoil is rejoiced over. Then he struck with his hand toward Sham and said: An enemy will gather against the Muslims from here. So they will meet, and a detachment will pledge for death and not return except victorious. So they will fight until the sun sets from here. So they will meet and a detachment will pledge for death and not return except victorious. So they will fight until the sun sets, each not victorious, and the detachment will perish. Then a detachment will pledge for death and not return except victorious. So they will fight until the sun sets, then these and these will return, each not victorious, and the detachment will perish. Then they will meet on the fourth day and kill them and rout them until blood reaches the fetlocks of horses. And they will fight until the sons of one father who used to count upon a hundred will be killed, not a man of them remaining. So what inheritance will be divided after this? And what spoil will be rejoiced over? Then they will conquer Constantinople. And while they are dividing dinars with shields, a greater alarm than that will come to them: that the Dajjal has succeeded among your offspring. So they will abandon what is in their hands, advance, and send a vanguard of horsemen. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are on that day the best horsemen of the earth. I know their names and the names of their fathers and their tribes and the colors of their horses."
"5256","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, al-Mutamir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, from Ibn Masud, he said: Whoever buys aflocked animal and returns it, let him return with it a sa. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting goods before they reach the market."
"5257","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are three, let not two converse privately to the exclusion of the other, for that grieves him."
"5258","Muhammad narrated to us, al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Awn ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Masud, he said: There were only four years between our Islam and our being reproached with this verse: {Has the time not come for those who believed that their hearts should be humbled to the remembrance of Allah and what has come down of truth}? And some of us turned to others: What have we innovated? What have we done?"
"5259","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah and Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from his father - Sufyan did not raise it, and Shubah raised it - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the sermon of need. Sufyan said: Indeed praise is for Allah. And Shubah said: Praise is for Allah; we praise Him and seek His help. Sufyan said: We seek refuge with Him. And Shubah said: We seek refuge with Allah from the evils of ourselves. Whomever Allah guides none can misguide, and whomever He misguides none can guide. And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then he recites three verses: {Fear Allah as He deserves to be feared, and die not except as Muslims}, {And fear Allah through whom you ask one another, and the wombs}, {Fear Allah and speak a right word} up to His saying: {A tremendous success}. Then he speaks of his need."
"5260","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from his father, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - I think it is Abdullah - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the heat intensifies, cool the prayer - or: from the prayer."
"5261","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Awn ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Masud, he said: When you are narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), think of the Messenger of Allah what is most fitting, most pious and most guided."
"5262","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that you are a messenger I would have killed you - meaning the messenger of Musaylimah."
"5263","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Mansur, from Khaythamah, from a man, from Abdullah: It was said to him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Remorse is repentance? He said: Yes. Mujahid said: Regarding killing a soul, if he regrets."
"5264","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, he said: I heard al-Nazzal, he said: I heard Abdullah saying: I heard a man recite a verse from the Book of Allah other than what I had heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I took his hand and brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I saw the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) change, then he said: Both of you are good, and do not differ about it, for those before you differed about it, then he mentioned destruction."
"5265","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Utham ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, he said: I reached Abu Jahl while he was fallen with a helmet upon him, and with me was a worn sword. So I began striking his head with my sword, recalling a striking with which he used to strike my head in Makkah, until his hand weakened and I took his sword. So he raised his head and said: Upon whom was the defeat? Upon us or for us? Are you not our little shepherd in Makkah? He said: So I killed him. Then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I killed Abu Jahl. He said: By Allah besides whom there is no god, did you kill him? So he made me swear three times. Then he stood with me to them and supplicated against them."
"5266","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Umarah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray a prayer except at its time for its appointed time, except that he combined Maghrib and Isha at Jam, and prayed Fajr outside its appointed time."
"5267","And from Sufyan, from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have permitted you to lift the curtain and hear me whisper until I forbid you. He said: It reached me that it is the secrets."
"5268","Muhammad narrated to me, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Masruq, he said: I was sitting with Abdullah when a man said to him: What is suht? He said: Bribery. So he said: In judgment? He said: That is disbelief. Then he recited: {And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed, those are the disbelievers}."
"5269","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Abu Said the freedman of Banu Hashim narrated to us, he said: Al-Masudi narrated to us, from Awn, from Abu Fakhitah, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: When you send blessings upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), perfect the blessing upon him, for you do not know; perhaps that is presented to him. They said: So teach us, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: Say: O Allah, place Your blessings, mercy and benedictions upon the master of the messengers, the leader of the God-fearing, the seal of the prophets, Muhammad Your servant and Your Messenger, the leader of good and the guide to good, and the messenger of mercy. O Allah, raise him to a praised station envied by the first and the last. O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and upon the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"5270","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Hanifah narrated to us, from al-Haytham - Abu al-Rabi said: meaning Ibn Habib - he said: Abdullah said: I did not lie since I accepted Islam except one lie. I used to saddle for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so a man from Taif came and said: Which mount is most pleasing to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So I said: The Taifi with a mark on its shoulder. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked it. He said: Then when he saddled it and brought it, he said: Who saddled this for us? They said: The one you brought from Taif saddled for you. He said: Return the mount to Ibn Masud."
"5271","Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Maruf ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Ibn Buraydah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the riding animal of one of you escapes in a desert land, let him call: O servants of Allah, confine it; O servants of Allah, confine it. For indeed Allah has one present in the earth who will confine it."
"5272","Al-Akhnasi Ahmad ibn Imran narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, and I heard him saying: Ibrahim al-Hajari narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed Allah is Odd and loves the odd. So when you clean with stones, use an odd number."
"5273","Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Mihsan Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Qays, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, from Ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The feet of the son of Adam will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about five: about his life in what he spent it, about his youth in what he wore it out, about his wealth from where he earned it and in what he spent it, and what he did with what he knew."
"5274","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Murrah al-Hamdani, from Abdullah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our Lord marvels at two men: a man who rose from his bed and blanket, from among his kin and family, to prayer, desiring what is with Me and fearing what is with Me; and a man who fought in the path of Allah and was routed, then knew what is upon him in flight and what is for him in return, so he returned until his blood was shed. So Allah says to His angels: Look at My servant; he returned desiring what is with Me and fearing what is with Me until his blood was shed."
"5275","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Jarir ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Nafi ibn Burdah, from Ibn Masud, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying - while Ramadan had begun: Had the servants known what is in Ramadan, my ummah would have wished Ramadan to be the whole year. So a man from Khuzaah said: Narrate it to us. He said: Indeed Paradise is adorned for Ramadan from the beginning of the year to the next, until when it is the first day of Ramadan a wind blows from beneath the Throne and rustles the leaves of Paradise. So the wide-eyed houris look at that and say: O Lord, make for us in this month husbands from Your servants, that our eyes find delight in them and their eyes find delight in us. He said: There is no servant who fasts Ramadan except that he is married to a wife from the wide-eyed houris in a tent of hollow pearl, of what Allah described: {Wide-eyed ones restrained in pavilions}. Upon each of them seventy robes, no robe of the color of another, and she is given seventy kinds of perfume, none of the scent of another. For each of them seventy couches of red ruby adorned with pearls; upon every couch seventy mattresses whose linings are of brocade, and above the seventy mattresses seventy thrones. For each of them seventy thousand maidservants for her needs, and seventy thousand servants; with every servant a dish of gold containing a kind of food, finding in its last morsel a delight not found in its first. And her husband is given the like of that upon a couch of red ruby bearing two bracelets of gold adorned with red ruby. This is for every day he fasted of Ramadan, besides what he did of good deeds."
"5276","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Masud, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat meat, then stand to prayer without touching a drop of water."
"5277","Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Layth, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself, so he said: Bring me something with which to clean myself, and do not bring me a bone nor dung. He said: So I brought him ablution water, so he performed ablution then prayed."
"5278","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Zubayd, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Insulting the Muslim - or the believer - is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief. So I said to Abu Wail: Did you hear Ibn Masud narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"5279","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked that we supplicate three times and seek forgiveness three times."
"5280","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not fitting for anyone to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"5281","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdur Rahman narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr as five rak'as, so it was said to him: Has extra been added to the prayer? Then he performed two prostrations after he had given the salam."
"5282","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdur Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Paradise is nearer to one of you than the strap of his sandal, and the Fire is likewise."
"5283","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdur Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from al-Bara' ibn Najiya, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The millstone of Islam will turn after thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven years; if they perish, then by the path of those who perished, and if their religion stands firm for them, it will stand for them for seventy years. I said: Of what has passed or of what remains? He said: Of what remains."
"5284","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdur Rahman narrated to us, from Isra'il, from as-Suddi, from Murra, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: All people will enter the Fire, then they will issue forth from it by their deeds."
"5285","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdur Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: O Allah, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity and sufficiency."
"5286","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdur Rahman narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Dharr, from Wa'il ibn Mahanah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to the women: Give charity, for you are the majority of the people of the Fire. A woman who was not among the prominent women said: Why - or for what or because of what - are we? He said: You curse frequently and are ungrateful to the companion. There is none more overpowering over resolute men than women despite deficiency of intellect and religion. It was said: What is the deficiency of her intellect? He said: He made the testimony of two women equal to the testimony of one man. It was said: What is the deficiency of her religion? He said: She remains for I do not know how many days without praying."
"5287","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdur Rahman narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Abdur Rahman ibn Abi Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from al-Hudaybiya he alighted at a stopping place and rested there at the end of the night. He said: Who will guard us? Abdullah said: So I said: I will. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will sleep, saying that two or three times, then he said: Then you may. So I guarded them until when it was near dawn, what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said overtook me, and I did not wake except by the heat of the sun on our backs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and did as he does, then prayed Fajr, then said: Indeed if Allah had willed you would not have slept through it, but if there be those after you, then thus it is for whoever sleeps or forgets."
"5288","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdur Rahman narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar, he said: I heard Abu Amr ash-Shaybani say: The owner of this house narrated to me - and he pointed with his hand to the house of Abdullah without naming him - he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most beloved to Allah? He said: Prayer at its appointed times. He said: I said: Then which? He said: Then kindness to parents. He said: I said: Then which? He said: Then jihad in the path of Allah."
"5289","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdur Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, he said: I entered with my uncle upon Abdullah ibn Mas'ud at midday, and he established the prayer, so we stayed behind him. He took the hand of one of us with his right and the other with his left, and placed us on his right and his left. When he had prayed he said: This is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do when they were three."
"5290","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Abdah an-Nasri, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah has not made anything sacred except that He knew that some intruder among you would breach it. Behold, I am holding you by your waistbands away from the Fire, lest you plunge into it like the plunging of moths or flies or beetles."
"5291","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Fudayl, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of arrogance."
"5292","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed the last one to enter Paradise is a man who walks upon the Sirat, stumbling once and walking once, the Fire scorching him once. When he passes beyond the Sirat he turns to it and says: Blessed is He who saved me from you; He has given me what He has not given anyone of the first and the last. He said: Then a tree is raised for him and he looks at it, and says: My Lord, bring me near to this tree so I may shade myself in its shade and drink of its water. He says: O My servant, perhaps if I bring you near you will ask Me for other than it. He says: No, my Lord. So he covenants with Him that he will not ask Him for other than it, while the Lord, blessed and exalted, knows he will ask Him because he sees what he cannot endure. So He brings him near it. Then another tree is raised for him, better than it, and he says: My Lord, bring me near to this tree so I may shade myself in its shade and drink of its water. He says: O servant, did you not covenant with Me that you would not ask Me for other than it? He says: My Lord, this one, I will not ask You for other than it. So He brings him near it. Then a tree is raised for him at the gate of Paradise, better than it, and he says: My Lord, bring me near to this tree so I may shade myself in its shade and drink of its water. He says: O servant, did you not covenant with Me that you would not ask Me for other than it? He says: My Lord, this one, I will not ask You for other than it. So he covenants with Him - while the Lord knows he will ask Him for other than it because he sees what he cannot endure - and He brings him near it. Then he hears the voices of the people of Paradise and says: My Lord, Paradise, Paradise. He says: O My servant, did you not covenant with Me that you would not ask Me for other than it? He says: My Lord, admit me into Paradise. Then the Blessed and Exalted says: What will make Me quit of you, O My servant? Would it please you that I give you the world and the like of it with it? He said: Then he says: Are You mocking me while You are the Lord of Might? Then Abdullah laughed until his molars showed, then said: Will you not ask me why I laughed? They said: Why did you laugh? He said: Because of the laughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5293","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Amr ibn Sa'id, from Humayd ibn Abdur Rahman al-Himyari, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: I was not kept away from three things - or not withheld from three things - from private counsel, and from such and such, and from such and such. Abdullah said: My uncle forgot one, and I forgot the other, and this one remained. Then I came to him while Malik ar-Rahawi was with him, and I caught the end of their conversation while he was saying: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man to whom has been allotted of beauty what you see, and I do not like that anyone should surpass me by two sandal straps or more; is that part of insolent transgression? He said: No, but insolent transgression is whoever belittles the truth and despises people."
"5294","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept on a mat that left marks on his side, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not permit us to spread something softer than it under you? He said: What have I to do with the world? My likeness and the likeness of the world is only like a rider who journeyed on a hot day, then rested under a tree, then departed and left it."
"5295","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talha narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Murra, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They detained us from the middle prayer until the sun set; may Allah fill their bellies and their graves with fire."
"5296","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talha narrated to us, with its chain, the like of it. (Repeated narration.)"
"5297","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed me, Jabala ibn Suhaym narrated to me, from Mu'thir ibn Afazah, from Abdullah, he said: On the night the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken by night, he met Ibrahim, Musa and Isa, may Allah's blessings be upon them, and they discussed the Hour, when is it? They began with Ibrahim and asked him about it, but he had no knowledge of it. Then they asked Musa, but he had no knowledge of it. Then they referred the discussion to Isa, and he said: Allah has covenanted to me concerning what is short of its appointed time; as for its appointed time, none knows it except Allah. Then he mentioned the emergence of the Dajjal: I will descend and kill him, then people will return to their lands, and Ya'juj and Ma'juj will confront them, and they are from every elevated place hastening, they will not pass by water except they drink it, nor by anything except they spoil it. Then they will cry out to me, so I will supplicate to Allah and He will cause them to die, and the earth will stink from their odor. Then I will supplicate to Allah to send rain, so it will carry their bodies and cast them into the sea. Then the mountains will be blown away and the earth will be spread out like leather. Then Allah, blessed and exalted, has covenanted to me that when that happens, the Hour among people is like the pregnant woman at full term, whose family does not know when she will suddenly give birth, by night or by day. Al-Awwam said: I found the confirmation of that in the Book of Allah, then he recited: Until when Ya'juj and Ma'juj are opened, the verse."
"5298","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan ath-Thawri informed us, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, he said: A man came to Abu Musa and Salman ibn Rabi'a and asked them about a daughter, a son's daughter, a paternal sister, and a mother, and he mentioned the hadith."
"5299","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from Simak, from Abdur Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah brighten a man who hears a hadith from us and conveys it as he heard it, for indeed many a conveyed one retains it better than the hearer."
"5300","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq informed us, Abu Salama al-Juhani informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Abdur Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant ever says, when grief and sorrow befall him: O Allah, I am Your servant and the son of Your servant, my forelock is in Your hand, Your decree concerning me proceeds, Your judgment concerning me is just; I ask You by every name by which You have named Yourself, or sent down in Your Book, or taught to anyone of Your creation, or kept exclusively in the knowledge of the unseen with You, to make the Quran the spring of my heart, the light of my sight, the dispeller of my sorrow and the remover of my anxiety, except that Allah removes his anxiety and replaces his sorrow with joy. They said: O Messenger of Allah, should we learn these words? He said: Yes, whoever hears them should learn them."
"5301","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, Abu Ishaq ash-Shaybani narrated to me, from al-Qasim ibn Abdur Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The millstone of Islam will turn at the head of thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven years; if they perish, then by the path of those who perished, and if they remain, their religion will remain for them for seventy years."
"5302","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Farqad as-Sabakhi narrated to us, Jabir ibn Yazid narrated to us, that he heard Masruq narrating, from Abdullah - perhaps he said: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that he said: I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so visit them; and I had forbidden you to keep the meat of sacrifices beyond three days, so keep it; and I had forbidden you these vessels, so make nabidh in them, but avoid every intoxicant."
"5303","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Asim, from Zir, from Abdullah, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your nation whom you have not seen on the Day of Resurrection? He said: They will be radiant with white marks, piebald from the traces of ablution."
"5304","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Fazara, from Abu Zayd, freedman of Amr ibn Hurayth, from Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the night of the jinn: Do you have any purifying water? He said: No, except some nabidh in a waterskin. He said: Bring it; a good date and pure water."
"5305","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abdur Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Alqama, he said: Ibn Mas'ud said: Shall I not pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Then he prayed with them and raised his hands only once."
"5306","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from az-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Talha, from Murra, from Abdullah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken by night, he ended at Sidrat al-Muntaha, which is in the sixth heaven; to it ends whatever is raised from the earth and is taken from it, and to it ends whatever descends from above it and is taken from it: When there covered the Sidra that which covered. He said: Moths of gold. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given three traits: the five prayers, the closing verses of Surat al-Baqara, and forgiveness for whoever of his nation does not associate anything with Allah, for the grave destructive sins."
"5307","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abdur Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a tent of leather among about forty men, and he said: You will have conquests opened for you, and be aided and attain spoils; so whoever of you reaches that should fear Allah, enjoin good, forbid evil, and join ties of kinship. Whoever lies upon me deliberately should take his seat in the Fire. The likeness of one who aids his people upon falsehood is like a camel in a well pulling itself out by its tail."
"5308","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Zir, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast three days from the beginning of every crescent, and he rarely failed to fast Friday."
"5309","And from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha prayer one night, then went out to the mosque, and the people were waiting for the prayer. He said: There is no one of the people of the religions who remembers Allah at this hour except you. He said: And these verses were revealed: They are not alike; among the People of the Book is an upright nation, up to: And Allah knows the God-fearing."
"5310","And from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately should take his seat in the Fire."
"5311","And from Hashim, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I been taking a close friend from my nation, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend."
"5312","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Abdus Salam, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Ibn Mas'ud: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast while traveling and break fast, and he would pray the two rak'as and not leave them, saying: He does not add to them, meaning the obligatory prayer."
"5313","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Zir ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: I used to cut tooth-sticks of arak for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the wind would bend him over, and there was something in his legs, so the people laughed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What makes you laugh? They said: The thinness of his legs. He said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, they are heavier in the Scale than Uhud."
"5314","And from Abdullah, he said: I was a youth approaching maturity, grazing sheep for Ibn Abi Mu'ayt, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr came, having fled from the polytheists. They said: Boy, do you have any milk to give us to drink? I said: Yes, but I am entrusted and I will not give you drink. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you have a young sheep upon which no male has mounted? I said: Yes. So I brought it to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held it, wiped the udder and supplicated, and the milk began to flow. Abu Bakr brought him a hollowed stone, and he milked into it and drank, and Abu Bakr drank, and I drank. Then he said to the udder: Contract, and it contracted. Then I came to him after that and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me from this speech - or from this Quran. He said: You are a taught boy, but he taught me. So I took from his mouth seventy suras which no one disputes with me."
"5315","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Sa'id ath-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in the shade of the Ka'ba, when Abu Jahl and some people of Quraysh said - and they had slaughtered a camel in the outskirts of Mecca - so they sent and brought its afterbirth and threw it between his shoulders. Fatima came and removed it from him. When he finished, he said - and he used to like three repetitions - he said: O Allah, upon You is Quraysh - three times - Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, Utba ibn Rabi'a, Shayba ibn Rabi'a, al-Walid ibn Utba, Umayya ibn Khalaf, and Uqba ibn Abi Mu'ayt. Abdullah said: I saw them slain in the well of Badr - or in a well. Abu Ishaq said: And I forgot the seventh."
"5316","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from al-Mughira al-Yashkuri, from al-Ma'rur, from Abdullah, he said: Umm Habiba said: O Allah, bless me in my husband the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and in my father Abu Sufyan, and in my brother Mu'awiya. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have asked Allah about fixed lifespans, apportioned provisions, and fully reached traces; nothing of them is hastened before its time. Had you asked Allah to protect you from the punishment of the Fire or the punishment of the grave, it would have been better - or it would have been more excellent. He said: Then monkeys were mentioned - he said: and I think he meant pigs - were they from what was transformed among the Children of Israel? He said: Indeed Allah did not destroy a people and leave for them offspring or progeny; and monkeys - and I think he said: pigs - existed before that."
"5317","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Abu al-A'yan al-Abdi, from Abu al-Ahwas al-Jushami: that Ibn Mas'ud narrated to them that they asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about monkeys and pigs: Are they from the offspring of the Jews? The Messenger of Allah said: Indeed Allah did not curse a people and transform them such that they had offspring until He destroyed them; but this was a creation that existed, and when Allah became angry upon the Jews He transformed them, so they became like them."
"5318","Shayban narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, with its chain, the like of it."
"5319","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Za'ida narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi an-Najud, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the worst of people are those whom the Hour overtakes and who take graves as mosques."
"5320","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman ar-Razi narrated to us, he said: I heard Bashir Abu Isma'il mention, from Sayyar, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is afflicted by poverty and presents it to people, his poverty will not be remedied; and whoever presents it to Allah, Allah will soon grant him sufficiency: either immediate sufficiency or deferred death."
"5321","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdus Samad ibn Abdul Warith narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Zir, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: that the nations were presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until his nation was presented, and their multitude pleased him. It was said: Indeed with these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning."
"5322","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdus Samad ibn Abdul Warith narrated to us, Abdul Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Mas'ud: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the remaining third of the night comes, Allah descends to the lowest heaven, then the gates of heaven are opened, then they are spread out, then He says: Is there any asker? And it remains so until dawn rises."
"5323","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Abu al-A'yan al-Abdi, from Abu al-Ahwas al-Jushami: that he said: While Ibn Mas'ud was delivering a sermon one day, a snake was moving along the wall, so he cut his sermon and struck it with a small staff until he killed it, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever kills a snake, it is as if he killed a polytheist man."
"5324","Shayban narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, with its chain, the like of it."
"5325","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mujalid, from ash-Sha'bi, from Masruq, he said: We were sitting with Ibn Mas'ud one night after Maghrib while he was teaching us the Quran, when a man asked him: O Abu Abdur Rahman, did you ask the Messenger of Allah how many caliphs will rule this nation? Ibn Mas'ud said: None asked me about it since I came to Iraq before you. He said: Yes, we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Twelve, the number of the chiefs of the Children of Israel."
"5326","Shayban narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, with its chain, the like of it."
"5327","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let those of understanding and intellect stand nearest to me, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Do not differ, lest your hearts differ, and beware of the clamors of the markets."
"5328","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, the like of it."
"5329","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdul Malik ibn Umayr narrate, from Abdur Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Behold, do not return after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."
"5330","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to recite: So is there any who will remember."
"5331","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, Aban ibn Abdullah al-Bajali narrated to us, from Karim ibn Abi Hazim, from Salma bint Jabir: that her husband was martyred, so she came to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and said: O Abu Abdur Rahman, my husband was martyred, and men have proposed to me; do you hope that if Allah joins me and him in Paradise I will be among his wives? He said: Yes. Some of the people said: O Abu Abdur Rahman, we have not seen you do this with any woman other than this one? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed the first of my nation to join me in Paradise is a woman from Ahmas."
"5332","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdul Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most beloved to Allah? He said: You pray the prayers at their appointed times. He said: I said: Then which? He said: Then kindness to parents. He said: I said: Then which? He said: Then jihad in the path of Allah; and had I asked him for more, he would have given me more."
"5333","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdul Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Sulayman al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim an-Nakha'i, from Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall enter the Fire who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith, and none shall enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of arrogance."
"5334","Abdul Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abdul Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, the like of it."
"5335","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Abdul Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdur Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fighting a believer is disbelief, and reviling him is transgression."
"5336","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdur Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to recite: Indeed I am the Provider, Owner of power, the Strong."
"5337","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa and Humayd ibn Abdur Rahman narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdur Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father and Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say takbir at every rising, lowering and standing, and give salam to his right and his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until I saw the whiteness of his cheeks. And I saw Abu Bakr and Umar do that."
"5338","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, he heard it from him, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said to people who stayed behind from Friday prayer: I have intended to command a man to lead the people in prayer, then burn down the houses of men who stay behind from Friday prayer."
"5339","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: It is not Abu Ubayda who mentioned it, but Abdur Rahman ibn al-Aswad, I think, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself and ordered me to bring him three stones. I took two stones and sought the third but did not find it, so I took a piece of dung and brought them to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He took the two stones and threw away the dung, and said: This is filth."
"5340","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq ash-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: I came to Zir ibn Hubaysh, and love for him was cast upon me, and there were youths with him. They said to me: Ask him about: Then he was at a distance of two bows or nearer. So I asked him, and he said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Jibril, and he had six hundred wings."
"5341","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ata ibn as-Sa'ib, from Amr ibn Maymun: that Ibn Mas'ud narrated to them: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be a people in the Fire as long as Allah wills, then Allah will mercy them, and they will be in the lowest Paradise. They will be washed in the River of Life; the people of Paradise will call them the Hell-dwellers. If one of them were to host the world, he would feed them, give them drink, furnish for them, cover them - and I think he said: and marry them - without that diminishing him at all."
"5342","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: We conversed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night at length, then returned to our families. When we came in the morning to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Tonight the prophets were displayed to me with their nations and their followers from their nations. A prophet would pass with three of his nation with him, a prophet would pass with a group of his nation with him, a prophet would pass with a small company, a prophet would pass with one man of his nation with him, and a prophet would pass with none of his people with him. Allah has informed you about Lut, and He said: Is there not among you a right-minded man. He said: Until Musa passed by me among a great multitude of the Children of Israel; when I saw them they pleased me. He said: I said: Who are these? He said: This is your brother Musa ibn Imran and those who followed him of the Children of Israel. He said: I said: My Lord, where is my nation? He said: Look to your right; and behold the rocky tracts of Mecca filled with the faces of men. He said: I said: My Lord, who are these? He said: These are your nation. He said to me: Are you pleased? He said: I said: My Lord, I am pleased. He said: It was said to me: Look to your left; and behold the horizon filled with men. He said: With these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise with no reckoning upon them. He said: Then Ukkasha ibn Mihsan, brother of Banu Asad ibn Khuzayma, stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to your Lord to make me among them. He said: O Allah, make him among them. He said: Then another man stood up, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ukkasha has preceded you to it. He said: Then he said that day: I hope that those who follow me of my nation will be a fourth of the people of Paradise. He said: So we said takbir. Then he said: I hope you will be a third. He said: Then we said takbir. Then he said: I hope you will be half. Then he recited: A company of the former peoples and a company of the latter. Then he mentioned to us that some believing men discussed among themselves, saying: What do you think is the deed of these seventy who enter Paradise with no reckoning upon them, until they concluded that they are people born in Islam who remained upon it until they died upon it. He said, in what he narrated to them until it reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: It is not so; rather they are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqya, do not take omens, and rely upon their Lord. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that day: If you are able - may my father and mother be ransom for you - to be among the seventy, then be among the seventy; and if you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the rocky tracts; and if you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the horizon. For I saw many people crowding together there."
"5343","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Zir ibn Hubaysh, from Ibn Mas'ud: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The nations were displayed to me at the Hajj season, and I saw my nation. Then I saw them, and their multitude and appearance pleased me; they had filled the plain and the mountain. He said: Are you pleased, O Muhammad? He said: I said: Yes. He said: Indeed with these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning; they are those who do not seek ruqya, do not cauterize, and rely upon their Lord. Ukkasha ibn Mihsan stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me among them, so he supplicated for him. Then another stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me among them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ukkasha has preceded you to it."
"5344","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abdul Malik narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abdul Malik ibn Maysara, he said: I heard an-Nazzal ibn Sabra say: I heard Abdullah say: I heard a man reciting a verse contrary to what I had heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I took his hand and brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Both of you are good. Shu'ba said: And I think he said: Do not differ, for those before you differed concerning it and perished."
"5345","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abdul Malik narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A banner will be raised for every treacherous one on the Day of Resurrection; it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so."
"5346","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abdul Malik narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Simak, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad or Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I met a woman in the garden and took from her everything except that I did not have intercourse with her, so do with me what you will. He said nothing to him, then he went away. Then he called him and recited to him: And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds; that is a reminder for those who remember."
"5347","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abdul Malik narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Simak, from Abdur Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of usury, its giver, its two witnesses, and its scribe."
"5348","And with it Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abdul Malik ibn Umayr, from Khalid ibn Rib'i al-Asadi, he said: I heard Ibn Mas'ud say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed your companion is the close friend of Allah."
"5349","And Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abdul Malik, from Abdur Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fighting a Muslim brother is disbelief, and reviling him is transgression."
"5350","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Sayf ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Mujahid say: Abu Ma'mar Abdullah ibn Sakhbara narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibn Mas'ud say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me the tashahhud with my hand between his hands as he taught me a sura of the Quran: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. And he was among us; when he passed away we said: Peace be upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5351","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from ar-Rukayn, from his father, from Abdullah, raising it, he said: Usury, even if abundant, its end becomes little."
"5352","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from ar-Rukayn, from his father, from Abdullah - or he said: from Ibn Mas'ud - raising it, he said: Usury, even if abundant, its end becomes little."
"5353","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Fadl and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of usury, its giver, the woman who joins hair and the one joined, and the one who legalizes and the one legalized for."
"5354","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, Abu az-Zubayr narrated to us, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Abu Ubayda, from Abdullah: that the polytheists distracted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Trench from four prayers until as much of the night passed as Allah willed. He said: Then he ordered Bilal, who called the adhan, then gave the iqama and he prayed Zuhr, then gave the iqama and prayed Asr, then gave the iqama and prayed Maghrib, then gave the iqama and prayed Isha."
"5355","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, al-Awwam informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad, freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Abu Ubayda, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No two Muslims lose three children except that they will be a strong fortress for them from the Fire. He said: So we said: O Messenger of Allah, even if two? He said: Even if two. He said: Then Abu Dharr said: O Messenger of Allah, I have sent forth only two? He said: Even if two. He said: Then Ubayy ibn Ka'b Abu al-Mundhir, master of reciters, said: I have sent forth only one? He said: Even if one. He said: That is only at the first shock."
"5356","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Khusayf, Abu Ubayda narrated to us, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us the fear prayer. They stood in two rows: one row stood behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one row facing the enemy. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one rak'a with the row next to him, then they stood and went and stood in the place of those facing the enemy, and those came and stood in their place. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them and gave salam. Then they stood and prayed one rak'a by themselves, then gave salam. Then they went and stood in the place of those facing the enemy, and those returned to their place and prayed one rak'a by themselves, then gave salam."
"5357","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abdur Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Isa ibn Abi Azza, from ash-Sha'bi, from Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut for the value of five dirhams."
"5358","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Mu'awiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'ida narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Zir, from Abdullah, he said: A black slave joined the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of him. He said: See, did he leave anything? They said: He left two dinars. He said: Two brands of fire."
"5359","And from Za'ida, al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, from Abdur Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, he narrated to them: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your permission upon me is that you lift the curtain, and that you hear my private speech until I forbid you. Al-Hasan said: As-siwad means private counsel."
"5360","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Mu'awiya narrated to us, Za'ida narrated to us, Sulayman said: I heard them mention, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, from Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your permission upon me is that you uncover the curtain."
"5361","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdul Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Hasira narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Abdur Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: How will you be with a fourth of the people of Paradise - a fourth of it for you and three fourths for the rest of people? He said: They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: How will you be with a third of it? He said: They said: That is good. He said: How will you be with half? They said: That is good. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection will be one hundred and twenty rows; you will be eighty rows of them."
"5362","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdala informed us, from Zir, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: We were on the day of Badr, every three upon a camel. Abu Lubaba and Ali ibn Abi Talib were the riding companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: When the turn of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, they said: We will walk on your behalf. He said: You are not stronger than me, and I am not less in need of reward than you."
"5363","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Zir ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, concerning this verse: And he certainly saw him in another descent. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Jibril at Sidrat al-Muntaha with six hundred wings, scattering from his feathers marvels: pearls and rubies."
"5364","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ata ibn as-Sa'ib informed us, from Murra al-Hamdani, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Our Lord, blessed and exalted, marvels at two men: a man who rises from his blanket and bed from among his family and people to his prayer, so Allah says to His angels: O My angels, look at this servant of Mine; he rose from his bed and blanket from among his family and people to his prayer, desiring what is with Me and fearing what is with Me; and a man who goes out to fight in the path of Allah while his companions flee, knowing what is upon him in fleeing and what is for him in returning, so he returns until his blood is shed. Allah says to His angels: Look at this servant of Mine; he returned desiring what is with Me and fearing what is with Me."
"5365","Abdul Wahid ibn Ghiyath and Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ata ibn as-Sa'ib, from Murra al-Hamdani, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it or similar."
"5366","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, Abu Ishaq said: He informed us, from Abu al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah used to say: Lying is not proper, neither in seriousness nor in jest, nor should a man promise a man something then not fulfill it for him. And Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Shall I not inform you of عضه? It is tale-bearing, spreading speech among people. And Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man keeps telling the truth until he is written with Allah as a truthful one, and a man keeps lying until he is written with Allah as a liar. Do you not see that it is said to the truthful: He told truth and did good, and it is said to the liar: He lied and acted wickedly. Truthfulness guides to righteousness, and righteousness guides to Paradise; lying guides to wickedness, and wickedness guides to the Fire."
"5367","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Abu ad-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The two eyes commit adultery, the two hands commit adultery, the two feet commit adultery, and the private part commits adultery."
"5368","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdala narrated to us, from Zir ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: that he used to cut a tooth-stick of arak for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the wind would bend him over, and there was thinness in his legs. The people laughed, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What makes you laugh? They said: The thinness of his legs. He said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, they are heavier in the Scale than Uhud."
"5369","And from Hammad, Ata ibn as-Sa'ib informed us, from Ibn Udhnan, he said: I lent Alqama two thousand dirhams, and when his stipend came out, I said to him: Repay me. He said: Delay me till next year. He said: I refused him, and took it from him. He said: I came to him after that, and he said: You have distressed me, and withheld me. I said: Yes, it is your deed. He said: What is my affair? I said: You narrated to me, from Ibn Mas'ud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A loan runs the course of half of charity. He said: Yes, it is so. He said: Then take now."
"5370","And from Affan, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrate, from Abdur Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: We performed Hajj with Ibn Mas'ud until when the first dawn rose, he stood and prayed the morning prayer. He said: I said to him: You did not used to pray this prayer at this hour? And he used to pray delaying until light. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray on this day, in this place, praying at this hour, meaning at Muzdalifa."
"5371","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Asim, from Zir, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray, and when he prostrated, al-Hasan and al-Husayn would leap upon his back. When they wanted to stop them, he signaled to them: Leave them. When he finished the prayer he placed them in his lap and said: Whoever loves me should love these two."
"5372","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not a curser, nor a taunter, nor obscene, nor foul-mouthed."
"5373","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sleep in his prostration; his sleep was known only by his snoring, then he would stand in his prayer."
"5374","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Shuja' ibn al-Walid ibn Qays narrated to us, Abu Khalid ad-Dalani narrated to us, from Talq ibn Habib, from Abu Aqrab al-Asadi, he said: I came to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud while he was on a roof, and I sat with him while he was saying: Allah and His Messenger have spoken truth, Allah and His Messenger have spoken truth. He said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us that Laylat al-Qadr is in the middle of the last seven, and that the sun rises on its morning without rays. So I ascended and saw it as such, and said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken truth."
"5375","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: And Abdullah heard of a landsinking, so he said: We, the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), used to count signs as blessings, while you count them as fright. Once while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and had no water, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek whoever has water. So we did, and water was brought. He poured it into a vessel, then placed his palm in it, and water began to gush from between his fingers. Then he said: Come to the blessed purification, and blessing is from Allah. So I filled my belly from it, and people drew water and were given drink. Abdullah said: We used to hear the glorification of food while it was being eaten."
"5376","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, with this chain, similar, except that he did not mention Alqama."
"5377","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave, when there was revealed to him: By those sent forth in succession. We began to receive it from him, when a snake emerged from the side of the cave. He said: Kill it. We hastened to it but it outran us. He said: It was protected from your evil as you were protected from its evil."
"5378","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughira, from Abu Razin, he said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Recite to me Surat an-Nisa. He said: I said: Shall I recite to you while it was revealed to you? He said: I love to hear it from other than me. He said: So I recited to him until when I reached: How will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you as a witness over these, his eyes overflowed with tears."
"5379","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn as-Sa'ib, from Abu Ubayda, from Abdullah, he said: Beware of these testimonies of martyrdom, that a man says: So-and-so was killed a martyr. A man fights out of zeal, fights while bold-hearted, not knowing for what he fights; fights for the world. I will narrate to you about that: The Messenger of Allah sent a company as an expedition, and they stayed only a short while until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Your brothers met the enemy, who cut them off; none of them escaped. They met their Lord and said: Our Lord, convey to our people that we are pleased and He is pleased with us; and I am their messenger to you: that they are pleased and He is pleased with them. So bear witness for the like of these."
"5380","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughira, from his companions, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, he said: I was with Abdullah at Mina, and when Uthman prayed four rak'as there, Abdullah said when he finished his prayer: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this place two rak'as, Abu Bakr prayed two rak'as, and Umar prayed two rak'as. He said: I think he mentioned what Uthman had prayed as two rak'as, then he said: Today he prayed four. Al-Aswad said: I said to him: O Abu Abdur Rahman, will you not greet from the other two rak'as and pray the other two rak'as afterward as supererogatory? He said: Disagreement is evil."
"5381","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abdul Hamid narrated to us, from Mansur, from Khaythama, from a man of his people, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no staying up at night except for one of two men: one praying, or a traveler."
"5382","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi, from Muhammad ibn Abdur Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not a taunter, nor a curser, nor obscene, nor foul-mouthed."
"5383","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Abu al-Jawwab ad-Dabbi narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Ata ibn as-Sa'ib, from Abu Abdur Rahman, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to seek refuge from the accursed Satan: from his madness, his magic and his pride. He said: His madness is epilepsy, his magic is sorcery, and his pride is arrogance."
"5384","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Qatada, from Usayr ibn Jabir, he said: A black wind raged in Kufa, and a man came whose sole refrain was: O Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, the Hour has come. He was reclining, so he sat up and said: The Hour will not come until no inheritance is divided and no joy is felt at spoils. He said: An enemy will gather against the people of Islam, and the people of Islam will gather for them - and he pointed with his hand toward Sham. I said: You mean the Romans? He said: Yes. He said: At that fighting there will be a severe apostasy; a detachment will pledge themselves for death and return only victorious. They will fight until night separates them; both sides return, neither victorious, and the detachment perishes. Then the Muslims will pledge a detachment for death that returns only victorious; they will fight until evening: night separates them, both return, neither victorious, and the detachment perishes. Then the Muslims will pledge a detachment for death that returns only victorious; they will fight until evening, both return, neither victorious, and the detachment perishes. Until when the fourth day comes, the remainder of the people of Islam will rise against them, and Allah will grant them victory over them, and they will be killed in a slaughter - either he said: the like of which is not seen, or he said: the like of which was never seen - until a bird passes by their flanks and nothing leaves them behind until it falls dead. The sons of one father, who were a hundred, will count themselves and find only one man remaining of them. So for what spoils shall there be joy, or what inheritance be divided? While they are so, they will hear of people greater than that: a caller comes to them that the Dajjal has taken their place among their offspring. They will leave what is in their hands and advance, sending ten horsemen as scouts. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know their names, their fathers' names, and the colors of their horses; they are the best horsemen on the face of the earth that day - or he said: they are the best horsemen on the face of the earth that day."
"5385","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiya al-Fazari narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud say: We used to go out to fight with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and had no women. We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not castrate ourselves? He forbade us that, and commanded us to marry a woman for a garment. Then Abdullah recited: O you who believe, do not forbid the good things which Allah has made lawful."
"5386","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abdur Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from his father Abdullah, he said: While a man was in his kingdom, he reflected and knew that what he was in would end, and that it had distracted him from worshipping his Lord. So he slipped out of his palace by night until he reached another kingdom. He came to the seashore and began to make bricks, living by it and worshipping his Lord. The king in whose kingdom he was heard of his worship and state, and sent to him, but he refused to come to him. When he saw that, he rode to him. When the worshipper saw him he fled from him, and he followed him on his mount. He said: O servant of Allah, there is no harm upon you from me. Then he alighted to him and asked him about his affair. He said: I am so-and-so, owner of such-and-such kingdom; I reflected and knew that what I was in would end, and that it had distracted me from worshipping my Lord. He said: You are not more entitled to what you did than me. Then he left his mount free and followed him, and they worshipped Allah together. They asked Allah to cause them both to die together, so they died together and were buried. Abdullah said: Had I been at Rumaylat Misr, I would have shown you their graves by the description the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described to us."
"5387","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'ba informed us, from as-Suddi, from Murra, from Abdullah - Shu'ba said: He raised it, and I do not raise it for you - concerning the saying of Allah: And whoever intends therein deviation by wrongdoing, We shall make him taste a painful punishment. He said: If a man intended deviation therein while in Adan Abyan, Allah the Exalted would make him taste a painful punishment."
"5388","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Azra ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: Umm al-Fayd narrated to me, she said: I heard Ibn Mas'ud say: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever says on the night of Arafa these ten words a thousand times, he will not ask Allah for anything except He gives it to him, except severance of kinship or sin: Glory to Him in whose heaven is His Throne, glory to Him in whose earth is His foothold, glory to Him in whose sea is His path, glory to Him in whose Fire is His authority, glory to Him in whose Paradise is His mercy, glory to Him in whose graves is His decree, glory to Him in whose air is His spirit, glory to Him who raised the heaven, glory to Him who laid the earth, glory to Him from whom there is no refuge except to Him."
"5389","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, Abdullah narrated to us while we were in the treasury, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were at Mina, leaned his back against a red tent, then began narrating to us. He said: None shall enter Paradise except a Muslim soul, three times. Then he said: Are you not pleased to be a fourth of the people of Paradise? They said: Yes. He said: Are you not pleased to be a third of the people of Paradise? They said: Yes. He said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, I hope you will be half the people of Paradise. I will inform you about that: The likeness of the believers among others is like a white hair on a black bull, or a black hair on a white bull."
"5390","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abida as-Salmani, from Abdullah: that a Jewish scholar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah will place the heavens upon a finger, the earths upon a finger, the mountains and trees upon a finger, water and soil upon a finger, and all creatures upon a finger. Then He will shake them, then say: I am the King, I am the King. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laugh until his molars showed, in amazement at what he said, confirming him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And they did not estimate Allah His true estimation, up to His saying: Exalted above what they associate."
"5391","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham, from Zayd ibn Za'id, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Let none of my companions convey anything to me, for I love to come out to you with a sound heart."
"5392","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ibrahim, from Alqama and al-Aswad, from Abdullah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I met a woman in the garden, embraced her, touched her, kissed her, and did everything with her except that I did not have intercourse with her. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent toward him, then this verse was revealed: Indeed good deeds remove evil deeds; that is a reminder for those who remember. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and recited it to him. Umar said to him: O Messenger of Allah, is it for him specifically or for all people? He said: No, rather for all people."
"5393","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a field in Medina while he was leaning upon a palm stalk of his. He came upon a group of Jews, and some of them said: Do not ask him. So they asked him, and he leaned upon the stalk as if revelation was coming to him. He said: And they ask you about the soul; say: The soul is of the affair of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except little."
"5394","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: When there was revealed: There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds, the verse, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was said to me: You are among them."
"5395","Suwayd ibn Sa'id and Abdul Ghaffar narrated to us, the like of it."
"5396","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Ja'da, from Abu Ubayda, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about Laylat al-Qadr, and he said: Which of you remembers the night of pale camels? Abdullah said: I do, may my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, with some dates in my hand with which I was taking suhur, while I was concealed from the dawn, until dawn rose; and that was the night of the twenty-seventh, if Allah wills."
"5397","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, al-Harith ibn Fudayl al-Ansari then al-Khatmi narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Abi al-Awja, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of Uthman ibn Affan, while Abdullah ibn Mas'ud was in Medina. Uthman went out and prayed with the people that prayer as two rak'as with two prostrations in each rak'a. Then Uthman left and entered his house. Abdullah ibn Mas'ud sat by the chamber of A'isha, and we sat with him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to pray at the eclipse of the sun or the moon; when you see it befalling, hasten to prayer. If it be what you fear, you will be in other than heedlessness, and you will have attained good or earned it."
"5398","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Ikrima, he said: Nabidh is ablution when we find nothing else. Al-Awza'i said: If it is intoxicating, ablution is not performed with it."
"5399","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ali ibn Ali, Yunus narrated to me, from az-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: A man came to him and said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say anything about horses? He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection. Buy upon Allah, and borrow upon Allah. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how do we buy upon Allah and borrow upon Allah? He said: Say: Lend us until our shares, and sell to us until Allah grants us victory. You will remain in good as long as your jihad is green, and there will be in the end of time a people who doubt jihad; so strive in their time, then go out to fight, for fighting then is green."
"5400","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, an-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: People used to recite loudly behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah said to them: You have confused the Quran for me."
